b.com/users/mbhamami/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbhamami","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbhamami/liferay-mfe/commits/094e0b2d07211dd18759566cb7d0e85a7cfb9d4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:02:29Z","email":"m.badr.hamami@gmail.com","name":"HAMAMI Mohamed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:02:29Z","email":"m.badr.hamami@gmail.com","name":"HAMAMI Mohamed"},"message":"feat(cx): 2e client extension ''BFF Card'' - appel d''un service externe authentifie\n\nPattern officiel Microservice Client Extension : le widget <lfr-bff-card> obtient via Liferay.OAuth2Client.FromUserAgentApplication(''lfr-bff-card-oua'') un JWT Liferay AU NOM de l''utilisateur connecte (app OAuth2 ''User Agent'', PKCE gere par le portail) et appelle GET /api/cx/whoami sur le BFF.\n\nBFF multi-emetteurs : nouvelle chaine de securite /api/cx/** validant les JWT LIFERAY via son JWKS (/o/oauth2/jwks, pas de validation d''issuer : iss=localhost non configurable) ; le reste de /api/** reste sur Keycloak. CxController renvoie l''identite des claims (userId, username) + marqueur servedBy:''BFF''. CORS etendu a l''origine du portail (localhost:8081).\n\nVerifie : 401 sans token, 401 avec token Keycloak (mauvais emetteur), non-regression Keycloak 200/200 ; widget deploye (bundle STARTED, main.js 200, portlet LXC_lfr_bff_card enregistre). Reste manuel : app OAuth2 User Agent (ERC lfr-bff-card-oua) via l''UI - type CX non gere par la factory CETConfiguration en 2025.Q3 (''Unknown type''), cf. RUNBOOK §9.b.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"61a9a11094534cb0b30ad57da924d8e6f3085867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbhamami/liferay-mfe/git/trees/61a9a11094534cb0b30ad57da924d8e6f3085867"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbhamami/liferay-mfe/git/commits/094e0b2d07211dd18759566cb7d0e85a7cfb9d4c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signatu