yload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/ccf15ab652d39eb17d7c035a199bde6d08c8edbb","node_id":"C_kwDOS1X599oAKGNjZjE1YWI2NTJkMzllYjE3ZDdjMDM1YTE5OWJkZTZkMDhjOGVkYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3","sha":"cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3"}],"sha":"ccf15ab652d39eb17d7c035a199bde6d08c8edbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/ccf15ab652d39eb17d7c035a199bde6d08c8edbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:44:29Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:44:29Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"message":"feat(telemetry): label the fallback, measure the free path (0.17.0)\n\nThe n8n workflow now stamps \"fallback\": true on the canned reservoir it serves\nwhen the model fails, so a caller can tell it from a generation instead of\ninferring it. refresh-pool.mjs refuses such a response outright and the PWA\nsays \"réservoir de secours servi\" rather than announcing a success.\n\nThe free refill path added in 0.13.0 emitted nothing, so its saving was only\nvisible as an absence of requests in the access logs. pool_refill and\nregen_fallback now go through sendTelemetry, one entry point holding the dev\nand opt-out guards that page.tsx used to inline.\n\nThe workflow''s own telemetry reached Axiom as application \"reservoir_idees\",\n\"action\" and environment \"production\": HoubaHouba looked like two applications\nand no query on application saw all of it. It now sends improv, event_type and\nprod. The repository had been right since ba0472e; that commit was never pushed\nto the instance. The three exported copies are realigned with it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fV5rSRdJsGac94D7KJsfk","tree":{"sha":"1cdfe881b015b668552f2bef3886517c11f8f622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/trees/1cdfe881b015b668552f2bef3886517c11f8f622"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/commits/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3","node_id":"C_kwDOS1X599oAKGNjNzIwMTUxMTUwMzZmZWU4ZDBlZWUzNThhNTFiNTAyMDI5ZmZiZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c","sha":"a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c"}],"sha":"cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/cc72015115036fee8d0eee358a51b502029ffbd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:27:40Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:27:40Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"message":"fix(pool): refuse the fallback reservoir instead of committing it (0.16.0)\n\nThe n8n workflow answers 200 with the mock hardcoded in its Check Error and\nMock node whenever the model fails, and over 39 runs it did so 18 times (46%):\nan empty model item, refused in 400ms or emptied after 30s. The body is\ncomplete and well shaped, so no caller could tell. Seven of the ten categories\nin the shipped pool are identical item-for-item to that mock, and the first\nscheduled run degraded emotions, locations and animals, which held real\ncontent the day before.\n\nA response with no new item is now a failure: the shipped items are kept and\nthe run exits non-zero, so the job fails visibly rather than committing canned\ndata. This is also why 0.15.0''s avoid block changed nothing on those calls -\nthe model never saw it.\n\nThree categories per run rather than ten, on a window that advances with the\nweek number (each comes round in ten weeks), and sixty seconds between calls\ninstead of 25: ten consecutive calls exhausted the free tier, and at 25 seconds\nGemini refused outright after two or three had gone through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fV5rSRdJsGac94D7KJsfk","tree":{"sha":"a72c5592b2fe4e447aaf51bbd2b0eac9a1847af6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/trees/a72c5592b2fe4e447aaf51bbd2b0eac9a1847af6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/commits/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c","node_id":"C_kwDOS1X599oAKGExMGZjNTRiMGYzMTNjNGNhODczMjYzN2I2ZDY4YmYwNGNiN2QxOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190","sha":"0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190"}],"sha":"a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/a10fc54b0f313c4ca8732637b6d68bf04cb7d19c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:12:48Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:12:48Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"message":"fix(pool): ask the model for items it has not already produced (0.15.0)\n\nTwo runs of the weekly refresh left 317 of 420 items exactly as they were\nbefore the job existed. scenarios, categories, echauffements and characters\ncame back item-for-item identical both times; emotions, locations and animals\nalternated between two stable lists. At temperature 0.2 with an unchanging\nprompt, the model returns its mode — the chain worked, it just produced the\nsame reservoir.\n\n/api/improv-regen now accepts an `avoid` array, rendered into the system prompt\nas a \"do not propose these, nor a close variant\" block placed before the\nfooter, which demands raw JSON and must stay last. refresh-pool.mjs sends the\ncategory''s current items and prints a novelty count, so a refresh that renews\nnothing says so in the log instead of passing for a success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fV5rSRdJsGac94D7KJsfk","tree":{"sha":"c2b09324c4b90ce3f4f6a206178ae56b8beb43a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/trees/c2b09324c4b90ce3f4f6a206178ae56b8beb43a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/commits/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190","node_id":"C_kwDOS1X599oAKDBjODU4N2JiY2M0ZGQ0ODYzNjAzMjExOTBjNThhZGFhNTEwMDYxOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole/improv-assist/commit/51d59031aca59206b7623c0a20f7007715ead364","sha":"51d59031aca59206b7623c0a20f7007715ead364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/51d59031aca59206b7623c0a20f7007715ead364"}],"sha":"0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/0c8587bbcc4dd486360321190c58adaa51006190"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gnueole","id":6651455,"login":"gnueole","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTE0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/commits/51d59031aca59206b7623c0a20f7007715ead364/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:44:44Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:46:09Z","email":"hi@eole.me","name":"gnueole"},"message":"docs: translate README, ARCHITECTURE and TILEAPI into English\n\nThese were the last three French documents in the repository, against a\nconvention that asks for English in every .md — and they are the three files\nthe root repo syncs into the Notion Engineering Hub.\n\nErrors found while translating, corrected rather than carried over:\n\n- The AI model section still described Groq / Llama-3.3 as the real-time\n  default. The workflow''s node is pinned to models/gemini-3.5-flash; the\n  model field the route forwards is vestigial and ignored. Said so.\n- The reservoir row claimed an empty pool reloads 50 items from n8n, which\n  stopped being true in 0.13.0.\n- The appendix links pointed at Architecture.md and TileAPI.md, which do not\n  exist on a case-sensitive filesystem.\n- The table of contents linked to #-changelog-historique for a heading that\n  reads Changelog.\n- The 504 section describes a Traefik network problem; a 504 on the regen\n  route is now a different thing and says so.\n\nThe submenu labels (Incarner, Inspiration, S''échauffer) stay in French: they\nare strings the UI shows, not prose.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fV5rSRdJsGac94D7KJsfk","tree":{"sha":"615b99ca156da3505a9fe49f0b3d174a274bdecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/trees/615b99ca156da3505a9fe49f0b3d174a274bdecc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gnueole/improv-assist/git/commits/51d59031aca59206b7623c0a20f7007715ead364","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6651455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnueole/followers","following_url":"https://a