er","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-d-j-i","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-d-j-i/wakeword-relay/commits/6645c2be370705303e4531a18d89b7e7d52abdce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T16:22:53Z","email":"aadjiman@gmail.com","name":"adji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T16:22:53Z","email":"aadjiman@gmail.com","name":"adji"},"message":"Add web_trainer milestone 5.5: tab UI + spectrogram visualisation\n\nFour-tab layout (Frontend · TTS · Augment · Train):\n  - Frontend tab: load any WAV → MicroFrontend → viridis heatmap canvas\n  - TTS tab: Piper TTS demo with per-sample spectrogram under each audio player\n  - Augment tab: load WAV, pitch/EQ/reverb/noise controls, before/after canvas\n  - Train tab: milestone roadmap placeholder\n\nwww/js/spectrogram.js:\n  - drawSpectrogram(canvas, data, T) — viridis colormap LUT, pixelated canvas heatmap\n  - audioToSpectrogram(samples, sampleRate) — resample → int16 → WASM MicroFrontend → Int8Array features\n  - _resampleTo16k — linear interpolation resampler\n\nwww/js/app.js — tab switching, WASM init, per-tab event handlers\n\nCMakeLists.txt — add HEAPU8, HEAP8, HEAPF32 to EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS so JS\n  can read feature bytes back from WASM heap for spectrogram rendering\n\nTests grow from 34 → 58 (all passing):\n  tests/ui.spec.js        — 16 tests: tab switching, controls, panel visibility\n  tests/spectrogram.spec.js —  8 tests: canvas dimensions, viridis colormap, audioToSpectrogram\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ffb401ab1eba49b17aba3b870974ba3733a6a39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-d-j-i/wakeword-relay/git/trees/8ffb401ab1eba49b17aba3b870974ba3733a6a39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-d-j-i/wakeword-relay/git/commits/6645c2be370705303e4531a18d89b7e7d52abdce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_ur