hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:00:04Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(graphql): add Phase 10 subtopics for Auth & graphql-shield (12/20)\n\nFixed the auth.ts main page''s own theory bullet claiming graphql-shield\nrules are \"memoized per request by default\" -- verified against the real\ninstalled graphql-shield@7.6.5 source (cjs/rules.js normalizeOptions())\nthat the true default cache mode is ''no_cache'' (no memoization at all),\nwith the page''s own codeTab already correctly opting into ''contextual''/\n''strict'' caching explicitly. Also added the already-verified\ngraphql-middleware/graphql-shield unmaintained caveat (reused from the\nsibling /graphql/resolvers finding) to the QnA comparing @auth directive\nvs graphql-shield.\n\n3 new subtopics under /graphql/auth/subtopics/:\n- graphql-shield Rules Are NOT Memoized by Default (fix-adjacent)\n- Contextual vs. Strict: Which Cache Mode Does a Rule Actually Need?\n  (gap-closing -- the precise mechanical distinction the main page''s own\n  codeTab uses but never explains)\n- graphql-shield Is Effectively Unmaintained (reused/tailored finding)\n\nWired all 6 touchpoints (routes, subtopics map, nav accordion,\nbreadcrumb, sidebar, search index). Build passed clean, browser-verified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88b3d214d6b8a01dc10d02dbf9d8392e051b6a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/trees/88b3d214d6b8a01dc10d02dbf9d8392e051b6a85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/commits/e916e5253b76e49d4371430dbe9f2ebf0a87e21a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20870970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/