pe":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/5348703951ef6a523b6e2d006d15ecc2d4c7c04e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:03:05Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:03:05Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(graphql): add Phase 10 subtopics for Subscriptions (9/20)\n\n- Tightened the federation QnA: it said \"Federation v2+\" -- verified\n  via Apollo''s own GraphOS docs that the real floor is Federation 2.4,\n  and that serving federated subscriptions through a self-hosted\n  router additionally requires a GraphOS Enterprise plan entitlement\n  (APOLLO_KEY/APOLLO_GRAPH_REF), never mentioned on the page at all.\n- 3 subtopics, each verified via direct execution against real\n  graphql-js: (1) the enterprise/version gap above; (2) a genuinely\n  surprising finding -- a subscription''s single top-level field\n  guarded by a variable-driven @skip/@include can make graphql-js''s\n  own validate() throw an UNCAUGHT exception instead of returning a\n  clean validation error, since validate()''s public signature has no\n  variableValues parameter at all; (3) the resolve function the main\n  page''s theory names but never builds -- confirmed it runs once per\n  SUBSCRIBER per event, with that subscriber''s own context, letting\n  one broadcast payload be shaped differently per listener.\n- SUBTOPICS key ''subscriptions'' collision-free, left bare. All 6\n  touchpoints wired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"342bfa20713a799d1c97d260d0a98a92f7affb0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/trees/342bfa20713a799d1c97d260d0a98a92f7affb0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/commits/5348703951ef6a523b6e2d006d15ecc2d4c7c04e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"