","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/bb2d47ea20aa3d81aa24156b7085628052adb992/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T03:38:17Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T03:38:17Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(graphql): add Phase 10 subtopics for Variables & Arguments (5/20)\n\n- Tighten two imprecise \"Variable Types & Defaults\" theory bullets:\n  * \"Non-null variables must always be provided\" contradicted the same\n    section''s next bullet and quiz Q6 (a non-null variable with a default\n    may be omitted). Rewrote to cover both cases + explicit-null rejection.\n  * \"Variable types must match the argument type exactly\" -- the spec''s\n    All Variable Usages Are Allowed rule is compatibility, not identity.\n    Rewrote to state the nullability-direction rule.\n- 3 subtopics, each verified via direct Node execution:\n  * IsVariableUsageAllowed modelled -- non-null var fits nullable slot;\n    nullable var fits non-null slot iff a default exists (var or arg)\n  * enum values: bare EnumValue inline vs JSON string in variables, with\n    the validation error each wrong form produces\n  * GET vs POST -- GET is query-only (safe method); real GET caching needs\n    Automatic Persisted Queries for URL length\n- SUBTOPICS key variables-arguments checked collision-free, left bare.\n- GqlNavComponent toggle wired. All 6 touchpoints wired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a880f39bd91