s/AjkKarthik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/d7d9c71087d1f3a720e8293d828e2ae7daf1fb67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T03:27:12Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T03:27:12Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(graphql): add Phase 10 subtopics for GraphQL Queries (4/20)\n\n- Fix one genuine main-page inaccuracy: the Directives theory bullet claimed\n  \"@skip and @include take effect on the client side -- the server only\n  receives the final included/excluded selection.\" They are evaluated\n  server-side during field collection, before any resolver runs; the client\n  sends the full query text unchanged. This contradicted the page''s own\n  codeTab and QnA.\n- 3 subtopics, each verified via direct Node execution:\n  * @skip/@include at field collection + the combined rule, with a Try It\n    on @include(if: $isAdmin) as (broken) access control\n  * the \"Fields in set can merge\" rule behind \"aliases are required\" --\n    fires through flattened fragments too\n  * the Lone Anonymous Operation rule + operationName selection -- why\n    merging query files needs every operation named\n- SUBTOPICS key queries checked collision-free, left bare.\n- GqlNavComponent toggle wired. @ escaped as &#64; in subtopic 1''s .html\n  text nodes. All 6 touchpoints wired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c0a001b16c09127eeef6446dc9c602ea1c845f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/trees/6c0a001b16c09127eeef6446dc9c602ea1c845f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/commits/d