s://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/fe055d11b76a51b4e24cf26035b77cd8db77d39d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:49:57Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:49:57Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(redis): add Phase 10 subtopics for Rate Limiting\n\n- Fix genuine off-by-one bug in the Sliding Window Counter Challenge''s\n  own reference solution: the Lua script''s remaining calculation added\n  +1 only in the REJECTED branch instead of the ALLOWED branch, so\n  every allowed request reported one MORE remaining than the true\n  value. Verified by tracing exactly `limit` (10) requests through the\n  reference solution -- the 10th (last allowed) request reports\n  remaining:1 when the true value is 0. Fixed the flipped ternary\n  (allowed == 1 and 1 or 0, not 0 or 1).\n- Add 3 subtopics: the-off-by-one-in-remaining-after-an-allowed-request\n  (fix-adjacent), implementing-leaky-bucket-with-a-bounded-queue\n  (gap-closing), fail-open-vs-fail-closed-when-redis-is-unreachable\n  (gap-closing).\n- Wire all 6 touchpoints: app.routes.ts (children array), subtopics.ts\n  (SUBTOPICS key left bare -- both ASP.NET''s and API Design''s own\n  rate-limiting topics were already proactively hub-prefixed), redis-\n  nav.ts (accordion toggle), breadcrumb.ts, page-sidebar.ts (tailored\n  content), search.service.ts (composite SEARCH_INDEX entries).\n\nThis completes the Redis hub''s entire Caching nav group\n(caching-patterns, eviction-policies, rate-limiting).\n\nRedis hub Phase 10: 16 of 21 topics complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cbf1a20d0b153c6f2a76e53837114d17bdc2507","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/trees/5cbf1a20d0b153c6f2a76e53837114d17bdc2507"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/A