m/users/AjkKarthik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/d79dbd3a239c7c79f8d3c81387a791f2080587ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:35:32Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:35:32Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(redis): add Phase 10 subtopics for Eviction Policies\n\n- Add an entirely missing eviction-policy family: Redis 8.6 introduced\n  LRM (Least Recently Modified) -- allkeys-lrm/volatile-lrm. Verified\n  directly against Redis''s own official Key Eviction docs. Added both\n  quickRef entries and a theory bullet naming the distinguishing\n  mechanism (only updates recency on WRITE, never on read).\n- Add 3 subtopics: lrm-evicts-by-write-not-by-read (builds the missing\n  family with a concrete access-pattern simulation showing LRU and LRM\n  pick the opposite eviction victim), the-lfu-morris-counter-formula-\n  verified (fetches Redis''s own evict.c to verify the real LFULogIncr\n  formula and the LFU_INIT_VAL=5 starting point), and\n  current-eviction-exceeded-time-and-other-info-fields (extends the\n  main page''s own Memory Pressure Alert Challenge with a real field\n  distinguishing a transient tip-over from sustained pressure).\n- Wire all 6 touchpoints: app.routes.ts (children array), subtopics.ts\n  (SUBTOPICS key left bare, confirmed collision-free), redis-nav.ts\n  (accordion toggle), breadcrumb.ts, page-sidebar.ts (tailored\n  content), search.service.ts (composite SEARCH_INDEX entries).\n\nRedis hub Phase 10: 15 of 21 topics complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a245711f748b7ca3739e5daa5f95dc1a5073d459","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/git/trees/a245711f748b7ca3739e5daa5f95dc1a5073d459"},"url":"https://api.github.com/re