b.com/users/AjkKarthik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/56a57acb099776da69434df23233e4c36d1d3d39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:18:15Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:18:15Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(redis): add Phase 10 subtopics for Caching Patterns\n\n- Fix genuine bug in the Stale-While-Revalidate codeTab: refreshInBackground\n  called fetcher() with no lock at all. Verified via direct Node.js\n  simulation that 20 concurrent stale-hit requests triggered 20\n  independent DB calls, reproducing the exact cache stampede the page''s\n  own \"Cache Stampede Prevention\" theory section teaches how to prevent,\n  just relocated into the SWR refresh path itself. Fixed with the same\n  SET NX EX mutex-lock pattern already demonstrated elsewhere on the\n  page -- re-verified the fix produces exactly 1 DB call for the same\n  20 concurrent requests.\n- Merge a genuine duplicate: the theory array had two separate sections\n  both headed \"Cache Stampede Prevention\" with overlapping bullets --\n  merged the one new bullet (server-side in-memory cache layering) into\n  the first section and removed the duplicate.\n- Add 3 subtopics: stale-while-revalidate-refresh-needs-its-own-lock\n  (fix-adjacent), implementing-read-through-in-application-code\n  (gap-closing), tag-based-invalidation-with-redis-sets (gap-closing).\n- Wire all 6 touchpoints: app.routes.ts (children array), subtopics.ts\n  (SUBTOPICS key left bare, confirmed collision-free), redis-nav.ts\n  (accordion toggle), breadcrumb.ts, page-sidebar.ts (tailored content),\n  search.service.ts (composite SEARCH_INDEX entries).\n\nRedis hub Phase 10: 14 of 21 topics complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree