ttps://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AjkKarthik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AjkKarthik/DevHub/commits/581c31057517f7cc4e94eec9833f20719d934599/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:04:54Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T02:04:54Z","email":"ajkkarthik@hotmail.com","name":"Ajk Karthik"},"message":"feat(redis): add Phase 10 subtopics for Streams\n\n- Fix genuine bug in Stream Metrics Aggregator Challenge''s reference\n  solution: it called XPENDING''s extended form (start/end/count args)\n  but its own hint claimed the reply \"returns summary with pending\n  count.\" Verified via XPENDING''s official docs and a concrete\n  50-entry PEL simulation that the buggy pending[0]?.[3] read (one\n  entry''s own delivery count) undercounted a real total of 50 down to\n  3 -- a 94% undercount. Fixed to call the summary form (no args) and\n  read index 0 as the total.\n- Add 3 subtopics: xpending-summary-vs-extended-form (fix-adjacent),\n  xclaim-vs-xautoclaim-manual-vs-scan (gap-closing), and\n  dead-letter-routing-by-delivery-count (gap-closing, reuses the\n  extended form''s own delivery-count field).\n- Wire all 6 touchpoints: app.routes.ts (children array), subtopics.ts\n  (SUBTOPICS key hub-prefixed to redis-streams -- bare `streams`\n  collides with the Node.js hub''s own /node/streams topic),\n  redis-nav.ts (accordion toggle), breadcrumb.ts, page-sidebar.ts\n  (tailored content), search.service.ts (composite SEARCH_INDEX\n  entries).\n\nRedis hub Phase 10: 13 of 21 topics complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3bf131612971ab26134859062394643d8f91624","url":"https://a