4e004cba686fe9370b560190f93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/0d33a684ad0254e004cba686fe9370b560190f93"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/98a55d85ce5b64b5ef9b1ff4ab15662d895234d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Make gravity scenario 2 a deployment you watch\n\neu-west starts with a dashed empty slot — no analytics machine. Scenario 2\nbecomes two beats: deploy-by-pull (the region agent pulls the analytics\nimage from its us-east origin across the WAN — digest, bytes, pull/boot\ntimings all from the agent''s artifact hooks — and the slot fills live) and\nthe existing co-located report, disabled until the machine exists. The\ncomparison panel gains the one-time-pull annotation, the lesson opens with\nthe pull-the-db anti-pattern callout, and the WAN link renders artifact\ntransfers as a packet train distinct from RPC traffic. Page reloads adopt\nthe agent''s deployed state.","tree":{"sha":"0fd4e413d456f1c3ee6fac52d834bf8b434e6150","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/0fd4e413d456f1c3ee6fac52d834bf8b434e6150"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/98a55d85ce5b64b5ef9b1ff4ab15662d895234d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/98a55d85ce5b64b5ef9b1ff4ab15662d895234d3","node_id":"C_kwDOS1qzxNoAKDk4YTU1ZDg1Y2U1YjY0YjVlZjliMWZmNGFiMTU2NjJkODk1MjM0ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b","sha":"096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b"}],"sha":"98a55d85ce5b64b5ef9b1ff4ab15662d895234d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/98a55d85ce5b64b5ef9b1ff4ab15662d895234d3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Rebuild page 01 around the lifecycle arc and a what-moves-where vocabulary\n\nThe page now reads as acts 01-06 with one question throughout — what moves\nwhere? A four-entry legend strip (attach / freeze-restore / pull-to-me /\ncode-to-data) gives every concept a badge + mini-diagram showing whether\ncalls, the artifact, or nothing crosses the wire and in which direction;\neach interactive card carries its badge.\n\nThe snapshot card and the pull story merge into one five-step lifecycle\ncard (boot -> freeze -> restore -> fork by pull -> fork again) with a\nlineage strip, three diverging counters, artifact wire-trace hops rendered\nfrom the pull hooks, and a one-line Phase 2 teaser. The compute playground\ncard is cut (its lazy-attach lesson lives in the other cards). The topology\ngains the artifact-cache node (hit/fetch flashes from real resolver\nevents), a local-machines group where pulled clones appear live with their\nartifact pipes (bytes / hit|miss / ms), and capability chips on machine\ncards whose manifests publish artifacts.","tree":{"sha":"0bc65a9cab4ec781486dff24509534ae201f1051","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/0bc65a9cab4ec781486dff24509534ae201f1051"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b","node_id":"C_kwDOS1qzxNoAKDA5NjIzNDUxODkyMWM3NDIwOTlkNDRlZTA3MTY1NmMxYjBiODczOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e","sha":"a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e"}],"sha":"096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/096234518921c742099d44ee071656c1b0b8738b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:20:28Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Fix lifecycle counter response shadowing and reap demo guests on shutdown\n\nThe per-target counter result overwrote lifecycleBody''s origin `value` in\nthe response (the UI showed the origin jumping when a clone incremented);\nit now travels as `targetValue`. Host SIGTERM/SIGINT disposes the lifecycle\nguests before exiting (with a close-timeout fallback) and demo-web gives it\na beat to do so — orphaned clones used to outlive runs, hold the fixed\norigin port, and wedge piped output. Also commits the lockfile for the\nmachine-analytics rsbuild devDependency.","tree":{"sha":"e4bc6caaf23f4f4ecc0294868c66d1e264854fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/e4bc6caaf23f4f4ecc0294868c66d1e264854fa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e","node_id":"C_kwDOS1qzxNoAKGE3MjY0ZTNlOTU5MGZlMGE1ZTM0MTliMDAwZWYxMjUwMTFhNTZiNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567","sha":"9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567"}],"sha":"a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/a7264e3e9590fe0a5e3419b000ef125011a56b4e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:53:31Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:53:31Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Drive the web demo''s lifecycle arc and deploy-by-pull from real artifact hooks\n\nPage 01 backend: /api/snapshot/* becomes /api/lifecycle/* and grows pull\n(fork-by-fetch against the restored origin on fixed port 3811, clones a/b\nwith a demo-scoped cache wiped on reset) and per-target counters; wire\ntraces gain an ''artifact'' event and attach provenance (pulledFrom), and the\ndashboard reports lifecycle + cache blocks fed only by onArtifactFetched.\n\nPage 02 backend: a ~140-line eu-west region agent whose whole deployment\nsurface is one machinen+pull entry; POST /deploy pulls the analytics image\nfrom its us-east origin (3806) through a WAN link (3896) and boots the\nclone at 3805 where the host''s existing WAN entry already points. demo-web\norchestrates the origin, agent, and two new WAN links (3896/3897), and the\nsmoke pass covers the full lifecycle round trip and deploy -> report.","tree":{"sha":"880f8120c585ef11c7ca626678e87259b3f6a10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/880f8120c585ef11c7ca626678e87259b3f6a10c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567","node_id":"C_kwDOS1qzxNoAKDljM2FlYTEwNjIxNTQ5NmQ1N2VhZjlmMmNhZTdlYzMwYWU5N2Q1Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76","sha":"ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76"}],"sha":"9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/9c3aea106215496d57eaf9f2cae7ec30ae97d567"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:53:31Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:53:31Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Bundle the analytics guest and publish its image artifact\n\nThe gravity deploy-by-pull story needs analytics_machine to be a pull\norigin: rsbuild bundles it (like apps/remote) so the published image is a\nself-contained guest program, and serveGuest gets imagePath so the manifest\nadvertises artifacts and GET /mf-image serves the digest-addressed bundle.","tree":{"sha":"8a69c8fb84a092f7d00e15174fd2f225286e2f29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/8a69c8fb84a092f7d00e15174fd2f225286e2f29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76","node_id":"C_kwDOS1qzxNoAKGVlNmJhY2M3YTc5MzI3ZDM2NGFlNDYxMDFiNmUyZjY4NzFjYjdiNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commit/0463d26e766057230aa44b5cf2717ccb187aa789","sha":"0463d26e766057230aa44b5cf2717ccb187aa789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/0463d26e766057230aa44b5cf2717ccb187aa789"}],"sha":"ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/ee6bacc7a79327d364ae46101b6e2f6871cb7b76"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/commits/0463d26e766057230aa44b5cf2717ccb187aa789/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:40:59Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:40:59Z","email":"zack@module-federation.io","name":"ScriptedAlchemy"},"message":"Re-center Phase 2 design on the MF runtime plugin","tree":{"sha":"88ff1451d77ee9e38caf5b624c7970dcd22ce7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/trees/88ff1451d77ee9e38caf5b624c7970dcd22ce7eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScriptedAlchemy/federated-compute/git/commits/0463d26e766057230aa44b5cf2717ccb187aa789","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"ver