":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/a154c1e58272060a1e4bd296f77c3382e8aa2fca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:21:32Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:21:32Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(roadmap): slice id S9B -> S18, the schema''s ids are S<n>\n\nroadmap-lint.mjs:101 enforces /^S\\d+$/ on slice ids. 0e7ab49 registered the bead-lane\nquartet as ''S9B'' to avoid renumbering during a concurrent-branch collision, and the linter\nhas been reporting it as a hard error ever since — fleet-wide, 1 error across 14 roadmaps.\n\nRenamed in place rather than moved: ids are immutable-by-convention and the block''s position\ncarries its PH2 grouping. A two-line comment records the old id so the rename is not silently\nlost. Nothing references #S9B outside this file — core''s status.jsonl has no entry and\ngrep across core finds none; the two remaining textual hits (implementation-notes deviation\n#20 and the dated fleet-navigator RFI response) are historical prose that should keep saying\nS9B, because that is what it was called at the time.\n\nS18 was free: S19 is the adapter slice filed in #49, and PH5 ends at S17.\n\nBefore: roadmap-lint 1 errors, 66 warnings. After: 0 errors, 66 warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c35478a574403f8b094d5ee28e806aee2dce50f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/c35478a574403f8b094d5ee28e806aee2dce50f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/a154c1e58272060a1e4bd296f77c3382e8aa2fca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojf