e":{"sha":"2fd085ff28263d87b23a46f216bc909211e4961e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/2fd085ff28263d87b23a46f216bc909211e4961e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/ef16730cac6ae94eed4957693a79deee3646610c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/ef16730cac6ae94eed4957693a79deee3646610c","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKGVmMTY3MzBjYWM2YWU5NGVlZDQ5NTc2OTNhNzlkZWVlMzY0NjYxMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a","sha":"0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a"}],"sha":"ef16730cac6ae94eed4957693a79deee3646610c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/ef16730cac6ae94eed4957693a79deee3646610c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:04:32Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:04:32Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(chat-store): an unreadable thread file must not read as an empty one\n\nA corrupt chat-threads.json took the SAME branch as an absent one — fall through to the\nv1 flat file, return {} when it is empty — and the next appendExchange wrote that {} back\nover the top. One unparseable byte silently erased every sibling thread. Live .data/ here\nholds three (leo, northstar:morning-cockpit, northstar:core) and the v1 file is already\n[], so the failure was reachable today, not hypothetically.\n\nAbsent and unreadable are now different cases:\n- ENOENT still migrates the v1 array into ''leo'', unchanged.\n- Unparseable, wrong-shape, or unreadable-for-any-other-reason moves the bytes aside to\n  chat-threads.corrupt-<ts>.json (renamed, never deleted — it is the only copy of those\n  threads) and poisons the store for the life of the process. Reads return empty; every\n  write refuses with an explicit reason. Both call sites already handle a throw:\n  routes/chat.ts:270 warns and drops the exchange, the clear route surfaces a 500.\n\nAlso retires the v1 file: once the migrated map is persisted, chat-history.json is renamed\nto chat-history.migrated.json so the legacy path can never fire twice. Retirement is\nbest-effort and never fails a write that already succeeded, but it is reported, not swallowed.\n\nFive regression tests (packages/server/src/__tests__/chat-store-corrupt.test.ts) pin the\nseam: quarantine preserves the bytes, writes refuse while poisoned, a v1-shaped array in\nthe v2 path counts as unreadable, ENOENT still migrates and then retires, and an ordinary\nwrite leaves sibling threads intact.\n\nRoadmap, in the same commit because they are the same slice''s bookkeeping:\n- S9 ready -> delivered. northstar.md `current:` is deliberately UNTOUCHED — the P3\n  movement travels as a `Movement proposal:` line in the PR body, which the merge ritual\n  owns (core TD-008). A slice session never writes `current:`.\n- S19 registered queued: deviation #15''s adapter work, which had no ticket anywhere.\n  adapters/delivery.ts:36 surfaces only northstar+roadmap PAIRS by design, so the Northstar\n  tab cannot tell \"no northstar\" from \"northstar without a roadmap\" (6 of 19 registry\n  entries). Filed as a slice, not a GitHub issue: this repo has never opened one, and its\n  own delivery pane reads roadmaps.\n- S13''s entrance cites the slice ref plus PR provenance; the -r2 number lands in a\n  follow-up commit once this PR exists.\n\nDeviations #19-#21 logged: the brief''s three \"sibling worktrees\" were PNG screenshots and\nthe merge commit was a no-op; the \"pre-existing\" roadmap-lint S9B error was latent because\nthe linter reads the working tree, which was two commits behind; and the running cockpit\nhas been serving with dolt-bead down on a stale S6-era COCKPIT_DOLT_PORT=3398 override\nwhile the real server holds 269 beads on the code-default 3307.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6df0a976650dce935a37982991d11173fdf53898","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/6df0a976650dce935a37982991d11173fdf53898"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKDAyNDNhZjhhZDE0MGM4ZmFiOGEyMTZiNGRkNDhmMTc4NGM3NzM5M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/59fd67a03df1a2d1289159cd8faedba7c59df2f6","sha":"59fd67a03df1a2d1289159cd8faedba7c59df2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/59fd67a03df1a2d1289159cd8faedba7c59df2f6"}],"sha":"0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/0243af8ad140c8fab8a216b4dd48f1784c77393a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/59fd67a03df1a2d1289159cd8faedba7c59df2f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:04:00Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:04:00Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(chat): PH4/S9 northstar chat tab — rebased onto main (rm:rm-l1-morning-cockpit#S9)\n\nContent-identical replay of 3805710 (PR #43) onto ce5e254. #43 went CONFLICTING after\n#44 (Cockpit v2 design bundle + PH5 roadmap) and #45 (S10 /api/fleet-structure) landed;\nforce-push is blocked for agents, so the branch is replayed rather than rebased in place.\n\nThe merge commit 6d0beb3 is deliberately NOT replayed: its entire contribution over\n3805710 was 0e7ab49 (S9B), already on main via #42, plus the roadmap union. Cherry-picking\n3805710 alone reproduces the branch losslessly.\n\nTwo conflicts, resolved per the standing rules:\n\n- .claude/roadmap.md — union of both sides, ids immutable, nothing renumbered. The phases\n  block keeps BOTH PH4 (this branch) and PH5 (main), in that order, and drops main''s now\n  stale \"PH4 intentionally skipped: a concurrent main-checkout WIP may be minting it\"\n  comment — this IS that WIP. Slice order S1-S9, S9B, S10-S17; PH4 prose appended after\n  the PH3 section.\n- implementation-notes.md — both sides appended deviations at the same position. Kept in\n  numeric order #14, #15 (this branch), #16, #17, #18 (main). Nothing renumbered.\n\npackages/shared/src/index.ts keeps main''s S10 fleet-structure exports alongside S9''s chat\nexports — additive on both sides, no loss.\n\nGates on the rebased tip: build, typecheck, contract:check, and the full suite green\n(shared 166, watch 64, server 44, renderer 24) with CORE_REPO set for the ADR-0013 drift gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f3302501ad1f17edfbc0617fc5dee91eb333ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/5f3302501ad1f17edfbc0617fc5dee91eb333ef6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/59fd67a03df1a2d1289159cd8faedba7c59df2f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events