l":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/8628db9eed8598ef43e476cc9f2c32294b26c44f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T03:22:36Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T15:43:15Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(motion): choreographed Section-00 swap — adapt IBM @carbon/motion curves (low-hanging fruit)\n\nThe F3 swap was a single flat 220ms fade. This makes it a composed, expressive entrance\nadapting IBM Carbon''s MOTION system — curves + durations + choreography only; the visual\nlanguage stays GroupThink/Rams-Lois (ADR-0001 — no Carbon components, no Carbon look).\n\n- tokens.css: a motion scale adapted from @carbon/motion — durations (fast-01 70 … slow-01\n  400ms) + easings (entrance-expressive cubic-bezier(0,0,0.3,1), entrance-productive\n  cubic-bezier(0,0,0.38,0.9), standard/exit-expressive). Attributed; motion math only.\n- app.css: the repo-keyed swap now choreographs instead of one fade — the block fades in\n  (fast expressive), the thread rail slides in (240ms expressive), the threads CASCADE\n  (80→200ms, productive), and the conversation follows (400ms expressive). A whole-section\n  re-scope is a Carbon \"expressive\" moment (decelerate-in); the small cascading threads use\n  the faster \"productive\" curve.\n- Transform/opacity only (no reflow jank). prefers-reduced-motion: reduce disables ALL of it\n  (instant) via .briefing-swap, .briefing-swap *.\n\nVerified via computed styles in-browser: rail 0.24s/delay 0.04s, threads 0.08/0.12/0.16/0.20s,\nconvo 0.4s/delay 0.09s, all on the expressive curve. Briefing tests (9) + typecheck + build green.\nRenderer-only, read-only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tud71dukYdZFz7ReUjdkMk","tree":{"sha":"d2dc2b58070d94a30958cc8f41535536e685b1cb","url":"https://api.github.co