":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/63699dd7bcbd96f8fee57077437bab8d8217b833/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T23:42:21Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T23:44:07Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(briefing): designed truthful empty First Move + honesty gate (F4)\n\nTrack F / Flow 01 / F4 (ADR-0012 #4). Completes Flow 01. F2 already made a quiet repo\nrender honest-empty; F4 makes it DESIGNED and distinguishes loading from quiet.\n\n- Briefing.tsx: split the !active branch into a distinct LOADING state (pulsing\n  \"reading the scan…\") and a designed QUIET state — an \"All quiet\" headline, a truthful\n  subline naming the repo + why it''s empty (no pickup/stale work), an honest footnote.\n  No fabricated thread, no fake affordance.\n- app.css: dedicated .briefing--empty / .briefing--loading treatment (editorial, centered;\n  reduced-motion honored on the loading pulse).\n- The suggested-entrypoints richer empty state (new threads / audits / integrations) is\n  DEFERRED to the operator design review — research/empty-state-design-followup.md.\n\nHonesty gate (the load-bearing part): tests assert a quiet repo renders the designed empty\nwith ZERO threads, loading is visibly distinct (not a false \"empty\"), and a populated→quiet\nswap leaks no threads — fabricated-thread rate = 0.\n\nRecords ns:l1-morning-cockpit#P3 45→55 (Flow 01 complete). Verified in a browser.\n\nTests: renderer 16 (Briefing 9, +3 F4), server 29, shared 76. typecheck + build clean.\nRenderer-only, read-only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tud71dukYdZFz7ReUjdkMk","tree":{"sha":"493195525f94b9e2d40ce686dd7c6541dcbd3094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/493195525f94b9e2d40ce686dd7c6541dcbd3094"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/63699dd7bcbd96f8fee57077437bab8d8217b833","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/63699dd7bcbd96f8fee57077437bab8d8217b833","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKDYzNjk5ZGQ3YmNiZDk2ZjhmZWU1NzA3NzQzN2JhYjhkODIxN2I4MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8","sha":"66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8"}],"sha":"63699dd7bcbd96f8fee57077437bab8d8217b833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/63699dd7bcbd96f8fee57077437bab8d8217b833"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T23:16:31Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T23:18:19Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"perf(briefing): deterministic-first + async SSE upgrade — kill the ~30s first-nav hang (ADR-0014 mitigation)\n\nOperator-flagged during the F2 dogfood: first navigation to an active repo blocked\n~30-45s on the Ollama briefing pass. This is the near-term mitigation from ADR-0014\n(the full materialized read-model is the separate captured initiative).\n\nNever block navigation on the model (ADR-0003): serve the deterministic floor INSTANTLY,\nthen push the LLM upgrade over SSE when ready.\n\n- briefing-generate.ts: briefingFrames() async-generator — yields the deterministic floor\n  first, then the llm frame only if the model actually beat the floor (quiet/off repo →\n  one frame). Unit-tested via the existing Ollama mock.\n- routes/briefing.ts: GET /api/briefing/stream?repo=&force= pipes briefingFrames over SSE\n  (sseInit/sseSend/sseEnd, mirroring chat). Per-repo cache reused. The non-stream\n  /api/briefing stays for agents / the GraphQL facade.\n- renderer api.ts: streamBriefing() over the existing streamSse parser.\n- Briefing.tsx: consumes the stream — first frame (deterministic) renders instantly, the\n  llm frame swaps in when ready; abort closes the stream on repo change.\n\nMeasured: stream first-byte 1.3ms vs the old blocking endpoint''s 45s. Browser: briefing\ncontent renders at 0ms (was a 30-45s hang); source badge shows ''deterministic'' then\nupgrades to ''✨ Chief of Staff''.\n\nTests: server 29 (+3 briefingFrames), renderer 13 (Briefing now streams; +deterministic→llm\nupgrade test), shared 76. typecheck + build clean. Read-only preserved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tud71dukYdZFz7ReUjdkMk","tree":{"sha":"096395e6e209d0cc19d17f899c445f6855a913ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/096395e6e209d0cc19d17f899c445f6855a913ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKDY2ZDgwMjRiZjRiMTE4MDQzM2U1Y2MzYzk1YWU0ZTQ4NTgwNmJiZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887","sha":"ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887"}],"sha":"66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/66d8024bf4b1180433e5cc3c95ae4e485806bbe8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:53:27Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:56:56Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"docs(adr): draft ADR-0014 — persistent precomputed read-model (kill 30s LLM recompute)\n\nOperator-flagged during the F2 dogfood: ~30s first-navigation latency. Grounded\ndiagnosis: the data/snapshot layer is sub-ms (already cached); the cost is entirely\nthe Ollama briefing generation (~30s/active repo, cold), and all caches are in-memory\n(lost on restart). F2''s per-repo scoping multiplied it (N×30s fleet toggle). Draft\nproposes a materialized read-model: persist derived views keyed by input content-hash,\nbackground-warm ahead of navigation, serve the deterministic floor instantly + upgrade\nvia SSE. Open questions: cockpit-local vs core-shared, substrate (disk vs Dolt),\nwarming trigger, near-term mitigation. Status: Draft.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tud71dukYdZFz7ReUjdkMk","tree":{"sha":"075e9ad85f1439470773154837b0f2e468d163d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/075e9ad85f1439470773154837b0f2e468d163d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKGRkYzJjMjI0NjlkMTg3NzU1MjIxYmU4YjhkOTIyOWUyNDViNWU4ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85","sha":"35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85"}],"sha":"ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/ddc2c22469d187755221be8b8d9229e245b5e887"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:47:57Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:56:33Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(briefing): animated Section-00 swap, reduced-motion honored (F3)\n\nTrack F / Flow 01 / F3 (ADR-0012 #5). The repo focus-swap was an instant content\nreplace (reads as a flash); F3 makes it a deliberate transition.\n\n- The Section-00 content area is keyed by repo (key={repo}) on both the populated and\n  the honest-empty returns, so selecting a Fleet tile remounts it and plays a brief\n  entrance (fade + 6px rise) once.\n- CSS @keyframes briefing-enter + .briefing-swap, using --gt-duration/--gt-ease (the\n  GroupThink motion language). Transform/opacity only — no reflow jank.\n- Adds the app''s FIRST prefers-reduced-motion handling: @media (reduce) zeroes the\n  animation (instant swap) for users who ask for less motion.\n\nThe Section frame (index/kicker/title) persists; only the content swaps (enter-only — a\ntrue out→in choreography needs a transition lib, deferred).\n\nVerified in a browser (Playwright): the swap container computes animation-name\n''briefing-enter''; the reduced-motion rule resolves animation to ''none''; keyframes present.\n\nTests: renderer 12 (+2 swap-container guards), shared 76, server 26. typecheck + build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tud71dukYdZFz7ReUjdkMk","tree":{"sha":"4e79204f0fb5a4aa785139caa9a4351e92c8bc49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/trees/4e79204f0fb5a4aa785139caa9a4351e92c8bc49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/git/commits/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85","node_id":"C_kwDOS19ny9oAKDM1Y2IwZTc2M2FhMWE2NGZlMTgwYjc1ZTIyM2ZlYzc1MDgzZDlhODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commit/6b716b93118bd5875180200a4b5ff82d14b40bb7","sha":"6b716b93118bd5875180200a4b5ff82d14b40bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/6b716b93118bd5875180200a4b5ff82d14b40bb7"}],"sha":"35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/35cb0e763aa1a64fe180b75e223fec75083d9a85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/commits/6b716b93118bd5875180200a4b5ff82d14b40bb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:37:52Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:40:03Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"docs(research): capture empty-state design follow-up (suggested entrypoints) for F4 + design review\n\nOperator input during the F2 dogfood: the Briefing empty state should ideally be rare\n(the cockpit drives toward no idle work), but when empty could surface suggested\nentrypoints — new threads / audits / integrations — turning ''no pending decision'' into\n''create the next move''. Honesty constraint carries over (entrypoints map to real verbs).\nA design-review item / likely its own later slice; F4 still ships only the plain honest empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claud