https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/80cd204508e496c653bc29754939b9baabccc17d","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDgwY2QyMDQ1MDhlNDk2YzY1M2JjMjk3NTQ5MzliOWJhYWJjY2MxN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/c8cbe27c87762b7aec345b1be257daa6f168ed4a","sha":"c8cbe27c87762b7aec345b1be257daa6f168ed4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c8cbe27c87762b7aec345b1be257daa6f168ed4a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0","sha":"509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0"}],"sha":"80cd204508e496c653bc29754939b9baabccc17d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/80cd204508e496c653bc29754939b9baabccc17d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T20:08:28Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T20:08:28Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(deploy): commit the Railway service configuration\n\nThree config-as-code files and the variable sheet that cannot be one.\n\nTOML rather than JSON because several of these settings need a reason\nattached and JSON has nowhere to put one. numReplicas = 1 on agent-worker is\nthe clearest case: a second replica would not share the volume, so its agent\nwould read a different or empty checkout, and it would also be a second\nRabbitMQ consumer competing for jobs in a pipeline that is not written to run\nconcurrently on one repository. A bare `1` invites someone to raise it.\n\nThe migration becomes a preDeployCommand on api rather than a manual step.\nThat is where it belongs, not where it is convenient: it reads EMBEDDING_DIM\nto size the pgvector column and that variable lives on the api service, so\nrunning it anywhere else is how the column ends up at a dimension nothing\nagrees with. It also fixes the ordering the runbook previously had to\ndescribe in prose — EMBEDDING_DIM must now simply be right before the first\ndeploy of api.\n\napi''s health check is /readyz, not /healthz. The shallow one answers ok with\nevery dependency down.\n\nAlso unifies the frontend build context to the repository root. It was the\nonly image built from a subdirectory, which is awkward on a platform whose\nconfig-file path does not follow the service''s Root Directory — the\nalternative was one service with a Root Directory and a `..` in its\ndockerfilePath. Removing the apps/frontend exclusion from .dockerignore\ncosts almost nothing: node_modules and dist stay excluded, which is where\nthe 227 MB was. Verified by building: 1.47 MB of context, and the image\nbehaves identically — gzip, cache headers, SPA fallback, and both\nenvsubst shapes with nginx''s own variables intact.\n\nStill nothing deployed. The files and the runbook are written from the code\nand say so.","tree":{"sha":"5e1a32ad768057fa8ec670891fd95acad8d41d53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/5e1a32ad768057fa8ec670891fd95acad8d41d53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDUwOWNjZGYwNjliNTkwOGUyYmQzYmUzMWJkMWZlY2Q2YTI4MzRjYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a","sha":"46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a"}],"sha":"509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/509ccdf069b5908e2bd3be31bd1fecd6a2834cb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:28:19Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:28:19Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(deploy): record PR 5, and the three limits it does not remove\n\nEight findings closed or narrowed, with the register updated from what was\nobserved. Three of them are marked \"mostly\" rather than fixed, and the\nreasons are written out rather than left in a commit message:\n\nDNS rebinding survives resolution checking, because git resolves the name\nagain when it clones. That needs egress filtering at the network, which on\nRailway is a platform capability this project does not configure.\n\nThe workdir cap is a trade. The agent reads those trees at query time, so\nevicting a ready repository''s checkout costs it read_file, grep and\nlist_directory until re-index while search and the call graph carry on from\nPostgres. Off by default for that reason.\n\nThe grep Python fallback can still block on one pathological re call,\nbecause Python offers no way to interrupt one. Everything countable is\ncapped, and the agent image installs ripgrep so the path runs only where it\nis absent.\n\nA closed finding that quietly leaves the hole open is worse than an open\none, so all three stay visible in the register rather than being struck\nthrough.\n\nThe runbook also now says to point Railway''s health check at /readyz rather\nthan /healthz, and to decide WORKDIR_MAX_REPOS and REPO_URL_ALLOWED_HOSTS\ndeliberately instead of inheriting defaults chosen to preserve existing\nbehaviour.","tree":{"sha":"8d532158eb0b2c5b6dd384b951ce228d1252e7e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/8d532158eb0b2c5b6dd384b951ce228d1252e7e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDQ2ODAwYWI5OWY3M2E3MjdiNjE1NTc2YWMyMWRjZGMwM2Q3YTgwN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb","sha":"7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb"}],"sha":"46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/46800ab99f73a727b615576ac21dcdc03d7a807a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:27:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:27:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(ops): bound grep, add a readiness probe, cap the workdir volume\n\nThe remaining three audit follow-ups, each with a limit stated rather than\nimplied.\n\ngrep had no ceiling of any kind. Its argument is a pattern the planner\nderives from a user question, and `.` over a large repository produced\nhundreds of MB of JSON buffered whole in the agent process, then serialised\ninto Redis and the SSE state. There is now a timeout (the clone path had one\nand this did not), per-file and total match caps, and a file-size cap —\nbounded at ripgrep rather than after the fact, since reading everything and\ndiscarding most of it is the behaviour being replaced.\n\nThe Python fallback is bounded on everything countable and is honest about\nthe rest: Python cannot time out a single `re` call, so a pattern with\ncatastrophic backtracking against one long line can still block the loop.\nThe agent image installs ripgrep, so that path runs only where it is\nmissing. The docstring says so instead of implying the fallback is safe.\n\n/healthz answered `ok` with Postgres, Redis and RabbitMQ all down, and the\nfirst user request discovered it. /readyz checks all three — all of them,\nnot short-circuited, because an operator wants to know whether one thing is\nbroken or everything is. It stays a 503 rather than a 200 with a body: a\nload balancer reads the status line.\n\nIt also checks the embedding dimension against the live column, which is\nthe one misconfiguration in this stack that produces no error at all\n(Deploy.md §5.4): the worker''s inserts fail, or dense search runs a stub\nall-zero query vector against real stored vectors and returns noise. A\nmissing table is skipped rather than failed, because before the first\nmigration there is nothing to disagree with and the Railway runbook starts\nthe API before running it. /healthz is left shallow on purpose — a liveness\nprobe that fails on a dependency gets the process restarted, which fixes\nnothing and loses the logs.\n\nCloned workdirs were never removed, for any repository, ever, so disk grew\nmonotonically with the number of distinct repositories ever submitted.\nEviction is a trade, not a cleanup: the agent reads those trees at query\ntime, so pruning a `ready` repository''s checkout costs it read_file, grep\nand list_directory until re-index while search and the call graph carry on\nfrom Postgres. So it is a count cap, off by default, evicting oldest-first\nbefore a clone and never the repository being cloned. An undeletable\ndirectory is logged and skipped rather than failing the index.\n\nAnd because that failure is now reachable, the agent''s missing-checkout\nerror says what happened: a bare FileNotFoundError sends the reader looking\nfor a missing file rather than a missing checkout.","tree":{"sha":"a9fa9f7c5be5cc2d0370b374b107f6fe01070870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/a9fa9f7c5be5cc2d0370b374b107f6fe01070870"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDdkYTgwY2RkMTcwZTZkYjVkZDlkYjg3MDJhMzNmM2NkYThhOTA1ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22","sha":"e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22"}],"sha":"7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7da80cdd170e6db5dd9db8702a33f3cda8a905fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:23:45Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:23:45Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(agent): key the tool cache by corpus generation\n\nThe tool cache key was (tool, repo_id, args) and carried nothing about\nwhich generation of the corpus produced the answer. Re-indexing a\nrepository therefore left every cached result addressable by the same key\nfor the next 24 hours, and the agent answered from the previous corpus.\nNothing failed, nothing logged, and the only symptom was answers that\ndisagreed with the index.\n\nThe worker already increments repos.index_revision in the same transaction\nthat replaces the chunks, so folding it into the key makes a re-index a\ncache miss by construction rather than by remembering to flush Redis —\nwhich is currently a documented manual step before evaluation runs.\n\n`index_revision` on tool_cache_key is keyword-only with no default. A\ndefault is what would let a new call site quietly reintroduce this.\n\nRead once per query and memoised on the state, not per tool call, so one\nwalk sees one corpus even if a re-index lands mid-answer. When it cannot be\nread — no session, no such repository, a query error — the request bypasses\nthe cache entirely instead of falling back to a revision-less key, because\nthat fallback would recreate the collision in exactly the case nobody\nexercises.\n\nThree tests cover it: same generation hits, a bumped generation misses, and\nan unreadable revision produces no cache entry at all. An existing caching\ntest needed a session stub, which is itself the change being made visible.","tree":{"sha":"36857f2e660074fcb7086dcbbfeb4b029e546b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/36857f2e660074fcb7086dcbbfeb4b029e546b20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGU4MjkwMjNhMzA4YTlhZWM2ZTgwZWViNWZiNmQ1YjZiODhmZjZiMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b","sha":"5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b"}],"sha":"e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/e829023a308a9aec6e80eeb5fb6d5b6b88ff6b22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:21:35Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:21:35Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(security): bound request bodies, harden clone, guard the internal key\n\nFour of the audit follow-ups, grouped because they are all \"an input this\nservice trusted more than it should\".\n\nRequest bodies had no size limits anywhere. QueryRequest.query had a\nmin_length and no max, so a caller could make the gateway parse an\narbitrarily large body into memory before anything rejected it; history was\ntrimmed only *after* parsing. Bounds are ceilings on abuse, not on use — no\nGit URL approaches 2 KB and the gateway already trims turns to 4,000\ncharacters.\n\ngit clone received the repository URL with no `--`, so a value beginning\nwith \"-\" is parsed as an option and `--upload-pack=<cmd>` is command\nexecution. The gateway validates the URL, but the worker consumes a queue\nmessage and should not depend on the only check being upstream of it. Also\nsets GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0: git otherwise waits for a username on a private\nor mistyped repository until the 180s clone timeout, when \"authentication\nrequired\" after two seconds is the better answer.\n\nINTERNAL_API_KEY had a working default published in this repository, and\nnothing but compose''s `${VAR:?}` stopped a service running on it — which\ncovers compose and not a container started straight from the Dockerfile,\ni.e. what a platform deploy does. Both the API and the agent now refuse to\nstart on the placeholder. The additional length rule applies only when the\ndeployment authenticates its users, which is a proxy for production rather\nthan a fact about it; that is stated in the code rather than implied.\n\nThe SSRF check only ever looked at literal IPs, so a hostname resolving to\ncloud metadata or an internal subnet passed. Every resolved address is now\nchecked, one private answer among several public ones is enough to refuse,\nand a resolution failure does *not* reject — a DNS hiccup is not evidence\nabout the host, and reporting it as an invalid URL would send someone\nhunting for a typo. Credentials in the URL are refused rather than\nstripped: a submitted URL is persisted and echoed back by the status route,\nso a token handed to this endpoint became readable by anyone who could read\nthat repository''s status. And there is now an optional host allowlist,\nempty by default, which is the only rule in the whole check that states\nwhat is *allowed* rather than what is obviously wrong.\n\nWhat resolution does not close is rebinding — git resolves the name again\nwhen it clones. That needs egress filtering at the network, and it is\nrecorded as unclosed rather than implied to be handled.\n\nResolution goes through a module-level seam so the tests do not perform\nreal DNS lookups; an autouse fixture stubs it, and the tests that care\nabout resolution replace it. Without that the suite would need the network\nand would occasionally fail for reasons unrelated to the code.","tree":{"sha":"9dc3f3cc556eb5e2a3b724bf6fd28ce576e4d4eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/9dc3f3cc556eb5e2a3b724bf6fd28ce576e4d4eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDU1MjFmZmFkM2M2M2EyNjNhM2FlNjk5Yzk3NTk3MDEyNzkzZmE3OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a","sha":"043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a"}],"sha":"5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/5521ffad3c63a263a3ae699c97597012793fa79b"},{"author":{"avatar_url"