nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/be3a1fceafa8e98e7e87295b15be9e345b031ede","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGJlM2ExZmNlYWZhOGU5OGU3ZTg3Mjk1YjE1YmU5ZTM0NWIwMzFlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65","sha":"797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","sha":"94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f"}],"sha":"be3a1fceafa8e98e7e87295b15be9e345b031ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/be3a1fceafa8e98e7e87295b15be9e345b031ede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:36:22Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:36:22Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(deploy): make the stack deployable on Railway\n\nFour platform constraints, one product gap, and two build fixes.\n\nR-1, the volume. A Railway volume attaches to exactly one service, and the\nworker writes the repository tree the agent''s read_file / grep /\nlist_directory tools read back. The two processes that share it now share a\ncontainer — via a Railway-only Dockerfile and entrypoint. docker-compose.yml\nstill runs them separately against a shared Docker volume: local Docker can\nshare volumes, Railway cannot, and that is a platform difference rather than\na reason to degrade the local path. The entrypoint uses `wait -n` so either\nchild exiting takes the container down; waiting on both in sequence would\nleave one that looks healthy while indexing is silently dead and every\nsubmitted repository sits in `queued` with nothing to explain it.\n\nR-2, the request limits. A query had no overall ceiling at all — only\nper-hop timeouts, so fourteen steps plus rerank and synthesis could outlive\nthe platform''s five-minute cut, and an abandoned request kept spending on\nthree metered APIs. There is now a budget that expires inside that window\nand emits a labelled TIMEOUT rather than a connection that simply stops,\nand heartbeat comment frames so a slow answer is not mistaken for an idle\none. `:` is a comment in the SSE grammar and the frontend parser already\ndrops those, so no client contract changed. Nothing half-finished is\nemitted on timeout: a partial walk has not been through the groundedness\nverifier.\n\nR-4, nginx. The site config becomes a template rendered by the image''s\nenvsubst, with NGINX_ENVSUBST_FILTER restricting it to three names —\nwithout that it would also substitute nginx''s own $host and $request_uri\nand produce a config that is valid and quietly wrong. The proxy target is\na variable with a resolver because Railway''s private DNS changes address on\nevery redeploy and nginx caches a literal target for the life of the\nprocess; the API would keep working until it was next redeployed and then\nfail with no change on this side. Defaults reproduce the previous behaviour\nexactly, so compose is unaffected.\n\nF-09, the product gap. GET /api/v1/repos, merged behind the localStorage\nrecents rather than replacing them: recents carry the URL as typed and this\nreader''s ordering, the server knows what exists. Without it a reader on a\nnew device opened an empty workbench and had to index something before they\ncould ask anything.\n\nAlso: gzip was off (the base image ships it commented out and this config\nnever enabled it), no .dockerignore anywhere, and HOST/PORT were baked into\nthe API image — Railway injects PORT and its private network is IPv6, so a\nservice bound to 0.0.0.0 there is reachable by nothing.\n\nVerified by building and running the frontend image: the template renders\ncorrectly under both the default and Railway shapes with nginx''s own\nvariables intact, gzip takes the main chunk from 760,088 to 269,497 bytes,\nhashed assets carry one Cache-Control rather than the two the first attempt\nemitted, and index.html is no-store. The list endpoint was checked against\nthe live local database. Heartbeats and the budget have five tests.\n\nNot verified: no Railway deployment exists, and the combined agent-worker\ncontainer has never been run. Deploy.md §10.2 is a runbook written from the\ncode, marked as such.\n\nDeploy.md §10.1 is also rewritten. Its setup block contained placeholders\ninside a copy-pasteable heredoc, that got pasted verbatim, and the\nplaceholder became the credential — the API refused to boot, correctly and\nwith the right message. The refusal was fine; the instructions were the\ndefect, so the block now substitutes its own values.","tree":{"sha":"50679f034ea912989fc04a63aac92b5dcdb8e954","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/50679f034ea912989fc04a63aac92b5dcdb8e954"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDA0M2VjOWE1NmUzMzQ4MTFjZjc1MzM3MWU4ODc0OWRjNTk4MTk4MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","sha":"94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f"}],"sha":"043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/043ec9a56e334811cf753371e88749dc5981981a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:08:28Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T05:08:28Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(deploy): write down how to see the auth gate locally\n\nThe two verification items that need a human need the gate switched on\nfirst, and nothing switches it on by default. That walkthrough existed only\nin a conversation, which means the next person rediscovers it.\n\nRecords the part that actually decides whether the gate can be tested\nlocally at all: apps/frontend has no .env, so VITE_API_BASE_URL is\nundefined and BASE_URL is the empty string, which makes the SPA call\nsame-origin /api/v1/* on 5173 with vite.config.ts proxying to the gateway.\nNo cross-origin request, so allow_credentials=False never comes into it.\nPointing VITE_API_BASE_URL at localhost:8000 breaks that, and the failure\nwould look like a cookie bug rather than a configuration one.\n\nPlus the three things that otherwise cost time: the Secure-cookie fallback\non plain-HTTP localhost, not hand-editing the hash back to $ separators\n(§2.3), and that make check is unaffected because conftest.py pins the\nsetting — which exists because a locally-enabled gate once failed four\nunrelated tests with no hint of why.","tree":{"sha":"be63a61b4c541241e022c2071624f32032e4d756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/be63a61b4c541241e022c2071624f32032e4d756"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDk0YzhiOTMxYTU3NTdiZjZmZTY5ZDI3MTBkMmFmZWMzYjg3MjA1MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc","sha":"ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc"}],"sha":"94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/94c8b931a5757bf6fe69d2710d2afec3b872052f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:30:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:30:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(deploy): gate the workbench behind a shared-account session\n\nDeploy.md D-2 and D-6: the landing page and the evaluation write-up stay\npublic, the product does not. One shared account, so no user table and no\nmigration.\n\nNo new dependency. passlib, pyjwt and itsdangerous are all absent from this\nworkspace and pulling one in to authenticate a single demo account would be\nthe larger change, so this is stdlib: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at OWASP''s 600k\nfloor, and an HMAC-signed session cookie that is HttpOnly, Secure and\nSameSite=Lax.\n\nThe gate is off by default, so local development, every current compose\ninvocation and the existing tests are unaffected. docker-compose.prod.yml\nHARDCODES it on rather than defaulting it — a production gate that can be\nswitched off by omitting a variable is not a gate — and the API refuses to\nstart when it is on but unconfigured, because an auth gate that fails open\nlooks exactly like one that works.\n\nAlso closes F-05: /docs, /redoc and /openapi.json enumerate the /internal/*\nsurface and are now off in production.\n\nA per-session daily query cap sits on /query alone. The login wall removes\nanonymous callers; it does nothing about a signed-in one looping a question\nthrough three metered APIs. It is counted before the agent is reached and\nit fails open on a Redis error, because a spend guard that takes the\nservice down when a cache blips has traded a bounded bill for an outage.\n\nTwo findings from verifying this, both fixed here and written up in\nDeploy.md.\n\nThe first is a real trap. Docker Compose interpolates `$VAR` inside\nenv-file values, so the conventional `pbkdf2_sha256$600000$salt$hash`\nreached the container as 22 characters with three of four segments eaten.\nNothing errored: the API booted, the health check passed, and every login\nfailed forever, indistinguishable from a wrong password. The format now\njoins on \".\" so the character never appears, and the hash is parsed at\nstartup rather than checked for non-emptiness, so any corruption stops the\nboot. This applies to every hand-picked secret containing `$`, not just\nthis one.\n\nThe second is that the test suite reads the developer''s .env, so `make\ncheck` is not hermetic. Switching the gate on locally failed four unrelated\ntests and the failures pointed nowhere near the cause. A root conftest.py\npins the settings whose defaults tests assert.\n\nVerified live on a gated container: protected routes 401, /healthz and the\nsession endpoints 200, /openapi.json 404, wrong password 401 with no\ncookie, correct password sets the hardened cookie and opens the gate,\nswitching it back off restores everything. Not verified: the /workbench to\n/login redirect in a real browser — it has four unit tests, but headless\nscreenshots do not work here and that is not a reason to claim otherwise.\nDeploy.md says who needs to look at what.","tree":{"sha":"2c29f5d1961a06221661aaf754c619feb50cefef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/2c29f5d1961a06221661aaf754c619feb50cefef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGViZmI4ZDAyYjE4NzdkZGY0MzEzYzk2M2JiOWZkZTdmZjExNGFjYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076","sha":"c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076"}],"sha":"ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ebfb8d02b1877ddf4313c963bb9fde7ff114acbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:09:56Z","email":"135147367+Odiethebest@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Odie Yang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:09:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #20 from Odiethebest/feat/managed-model-providers\n\nfeat(deploy): reach the same models through hosted APIs","tree":{"sha":"0f07cb6a482514ea75167846b34b5dd9c072e465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/0f07cb6a482514ea75167846b34b5dd9c072e465"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f07cb6a482514ea75167846b34b5dd9c072e465\nparent ca18b4a190b3095af75fc06f66070695923f2139\nparent c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076\nauthor Odie Yang <135147367+Odiethebest@users.noreply.github.com> 1785726596 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785726596 -0700\n\nMerge pull request #20 from Odiethebest/feat/managed-model-providers\n\nfeat(deploy): reach the same models through hosted APIs","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcAaECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOy0QAE8rfrcuVoOcZk1vwyeszBTE\n9gIQk2O0sPR/zicGT38+4vyJyEUslYm1ovcDzN1aLWb0Cm/u2JrbdlRC7G7t6Gi4\nGB51lbN1WLquQOH3ZN5xZDh6EWS7cnoxgV2ekAR2ULzWgcx+vvSjpNMGiMGyJHhy\nKaVv8734rh+xWERFuG/ifj+z/LTkundmUONZl882BLHwXIj6SFKzTp6rEZxNJr3p\nV84sDfh8KK9cErh7jvy2zLkOy6L0OI9mVCNkVx+JUIEIv+b5w47Ta5YPVkHBVh/Y\niR4xmFgft64K8LOBz02pZuJcsLF2iq6p/u8exzNN9vnMDb1UfNDiRSToHMYCot7k\nIWRjsGrHMHOTYZ+kVrBQwW1PtNTISf8THC+p9Ky20SAKHJA/NIi36X7jqYEN9