42746367bc039fb281aea076"}],"sha":"797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/797bb1e6e13373c69640fbd82131c5fdae43de65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:07:15Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:07:15Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(deploy): record the live cross-path verification of PR 2\n\nThe running stack was switched to both hosted providers and queried against\nthe existing 768-dimension index — the one the local sidecar wrote. That\ncombination is the parity claim itself: a query vector from Jina''s API\nsearching vectors produced by the local model.\n\nDense retrieval returned an identical ranking, the same five chunks in the\nsame order, with cosine differing in the third decimal (0.5155 -> 0.5182).\nHybrid returned the same five with the top two swapped, and those two were\ntied at 0.0042 in the baseline; the hosted run broke the tie 0.0043/0.0042.\nA tie broken differently is not a behaviour change and is not reported as\none.\n\nThe full agent path then reproduced the documented sidecar run citation for\ncitation: sessions.py:186 and sessions.py:557, both verified, groundedness\n1.0, three tool calls. Hosted BGE also returns scores in the same magnitude\nband as the local BGE sidecar, where the Qwen reranker on SiliconFlow''s\nother platform returned two orders of magnitude higher on a comparable\nquery — circumstantial, but it is the kind of evidence available.\n\nThe third-decimal drift is the caveat §2 already recorded: same weights,\ndifferent serving stack, not bit-identical. It is visible and it does not\nmove the ranking.\n\nTwo gaps are named rather than glossed. No index has been built through the\nhosted provider, so the bulk-embedding path — 23 requests, rate limiting,\nthe embed stage''s Redis cache interaction — is still unproven; that is\ndeliberate, because re-indexing would replace the verified reference index,\nand it will happen at the first Railway index. And the sidecar path was not\nre-run live after the switch: its code is untouched and its selection is\ncovered by tests, but that is a weaker claim than having watched it work,\nso it is stated as the weaker one.","tree":{"sha":"0f07cb6a482514ea75167846b34b5dd9c072e465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/0f07cb6a482514ea75167846b34b5dd9c072e465"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGM1MDY1YWU2MWM0M2IzNzc0Mjc0NjM2N2JjMDM5ZmIyODFhZWEwNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/42368cb3e8a9924d571072f7ea94530baf912360","sha":"42368cb3e8a9924d571072f7ea94530baf912360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/42368cb3e8a9924d571072f7ea94530baf912360"}],"sha":"c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c5065ae61c43b37742746367bc039fb281aea076"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/42368cb3e8a9924d571072f7ea94530baf912360/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:59:40Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:59:40Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(deploy): reach the same models through hosted APIs\n\nAdds a second way to reach the embedding and reranker models: Jina AI''s\nhosted endpoint and SiliconFlow''s, selected by EMBEDDING_PROVIDER and\nRERANKER_PROVIDER. Both default to `sidecar`, so no existing .env, test or\ncompose invocation changes behaviour, and apps/embedding, apps/reranker,\nthe compose profiles, the host scripts and both HttpXClient classes are\nuntouched.\n\nThe models do not change. jina-embeddings-v2-base-code at 768 dimensions\nand BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 are what the recorded evaluation measured, and\nevery figure the UI displays is a claim about that configuration. The\nprovider selects how a model is reached, never which one runs.\n\nBoth wire formats were observed against the live APIs before any client was\nwritten, and both differed from the sidecar contract in the same\nload-bearing way: results are identified by a per-item `index` and do not\narrive in input order. A three-document rerank probe came back [1, 0, 2].\nZipping arrival order against the input would attach the wrong embedding to\na chunk, or score every passage with another passage''s relevance — no\nerror, no log line, just worse retrieval. Both clients place results by\nindex and reject a response that is short, duplicated, or out of range.\n\n429 is retryable here and is not in the sidecar clients. A service we run\ndoes not rate-limit us; a metered one does, and on a free tier it is the\nnormal response under load. 401 stays non-retryable and surfaces on the\nfirst attempt, because a wrong key does not improve by asking again.\n\nTwo findings worth the reader''s time, both in Deploy.md. SiliconFlow runs\ntwo independent platforms: .cn serves BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3, .com served\nonly Qwen rerankers, and keys are not interchangeable — the failure reads\nas a bad key in one direction and a missing model in the other. Taking the\n.com path would have meant deploying a Qwen reranker under BGE''s measured\nnumbers, which §2 does not permit.\n\nVerification, stated precisely. 21 mocked-transport tests cover reordering,\ncross-batch ordering, every malformed-response branch, both retry\npolicies, provider selection and stub short-circuiting; CI stays keyless.\nThe production classes were then run against both live APIs: 5 inputs over\n3 batches returned 5 distinct non-zero 768-dim vectors, and re-embedding\ninput 2 alone landed 0.000000 from its batched slot against 0.586 for the\nnearest other slot, which is what makes the ordering claim a measurement\nrather than an assertion.\n\nNot done: no index has been built through the hosted provider. 726 chunks\nat batch 32 is where rate limiting and the embed stage''s Redis cache\ninteraction would appear, and neither has been exercised. This commit\nproves the clients are correct, not that an index built through them is.\nDeploy.md marks PR 2 acceptance as partially met for that reason.","tree":{"sha":"269cf48a67be164aeb500a1da1870862cdbd9118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/269cf48a67be164aeb500a1da1870862cdbd9118"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/42368cb3e8a9924d571072f7ea94530baf912360","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"commi