","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/9874f0bb83dc2e69e37e6c7a816203e43dcb5dd9","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDk4NzRmMGJiODNkYzJlNjllMzdlNmM3YTgxNjIwM2U0M2RjYjVkZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0","sha":"a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","sha":"d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b"}],"sha":"9874f0bb83dc2e69e37e6c7a816203e43dcb5dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/9874f0bb83dc2e69e37e6c7a816203e43dcb5dd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c0a9fdabfe4bb622145dceb75247e563173880dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:14:42Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:14:42Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(deploy): give every service the retrieval settings it reads\n\nThe production compose file configured almost none of the retrieval stack,\nand the failure mode is silence rather than an error.\n\nThe api service had no embedding or reranker configuration at all. Two\nconsequences. `make prod-migrate` runs alembic inside that container, and\n001_initial_schema reads shared_settings.embedding_dim to size the pgvector\ncolumn — so production built a vector(1024) column whatever .env.production\nsaid, while the worker inserted at its own configured dimension. And the\napi is the service that embeds the search query and reranks candidates, so\nit silently ran the stub path: an all-zero query vector against real stored\nvectors, which is dense retrieval returning noise with nothing in the log.\n\nThe other two services were short as well. The worker had a model and a\ndimension but no EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT, so it could not reach a service. The\nagent had RERANKER_ENDPOINT alone, which selects nothing — create_reranker_\nclient returns None for a stub model regardless of the endpoint — so the\nevidence-union rerank the agent performs was identity ordering in\nproduction.\n\nEMBEDDING_DIM is now required in production rather than defaulted. It is\nnot only the migration that depends on it: dcode_shared.db.models binds the\nchunks.embedding column type at import time, so every service touching the\nORM needs it right. A wrong value is a re-index, not a slow query, and that\nis not a thing to inherit from a default that happens to suit stub vectors.\n\nAlso here: the dead RERANKER_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9999 default is\nreplaced by an empty one, which fails loudly for a real model and is\nignored by a stub; the two documented compose invocations are reconciled on\nthe standalone form, because the overlay form the env example documented\nrepublishes Postgres, Redis and the RabbitMQ UI to the host.\n\nEMBEDDING_TIMEOUT_SECONDS becomes env-tunable instead of hardcoded at 300s.\nThe value is unchanged. Twelve retries against a 300s timeout can hold one\nbatch for about an hour while prefetch_count=1 stalls the queue behind it,\nbut those defaults are correct for a cold CPU sidecar; the path they are\nwrong for is the hosted API, which does not exist until PR 2. PR 2 sets\nthem.\n\nThree tests pin all of this, and each was confirmed to fail when its defect\nis put back. They parse the compose file by hand rather than importing\nPyYAML, which is only a transitive dependency here and is imported by no\nother code in the repository.\n\nDeploy.md records a correction: F-02 was written as \"the api service has no\nembedding configuration\" and was wider than that. The register and the\nacceptance criteria are updated from what was observed, not from what was\nplanned.","tree":{"sha":"b88ae0aed7fbfcd36a2e4a766fe0c2cb1b5b8014","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/b88ae0aed7fbfcd36a2e4a766fe0c2cb1b5b8014"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/c0a9fdabfe4bb622145dceb75247e563173880dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/c0a9fdabfe4bb622145dceb75247e563173880dd","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGMwYTlmZGFiZmU0YmI2MjIxNDVkY2ViNzUyNDdlNTYzMTczODgwZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","sha":"d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b"}],"sha":"c0a9fdabfe4bb622145dceb75247e563173880dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/c0a9fdabfe4bb622145dceb75247e563173880dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:02:52Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:02:52Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(deploy): resolve the two open questions that blocked PR 2 and PR 3\n\nD-5: explicit per-provider client classes rather than a generic\nOpenAI-compatible adapter. Neither Jina''s embeddings response nor\nSiliconFlow''s rerank response is OpenAI-shaped in the part that matters —\nboth carry per-item indices that have to be mapped back to input order — so\na shared abstraction would have to model the difference anyway. The cost is\nrecorded: a fourth provider later means writing a class, not setting a\nvariable.\n\nD-6: one shared account read from the environment. No user table, no\nmigration. The consequences are written down rather than discovered later:\nthe daily query cap becomes per session rather than per person, and a\nshared password cannot be revoked for one holder, only rotated. That is\nadequate for a gated demo and is not an authorization model.\n\nOpen questions drop from five to two. Team ownership stays unresolved and\nis the reason this branch is being pushed; the durable fix for the Railway\nshared-volume constraint stays deferred and recorded.","tree":{"sha":"4af233780b03905dd9511048da6ca3f6cbfb5598","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/4af233780b03905dd9511048da6ca3f6cbfb5598"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGQxNjI0MjZhZjA2YTZjOTk4YjJhMDc0ZmIzM2YxOWM2ZmNjYzdlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/3b9f977bf74cf102b2f4b419e59e2a75dc6ed313","sha":"3b9f977bf74cf102b2f4b419e59e2a75dc6ed313","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/3b9f977bf74cf102b2f4b419e59e2a75dc6ed313"}],"sha":"d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d162426af06a6c998b2a074fb33f19c6fccc7e7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/3b9f977bf74cf102b2f4b419e59e2a75dc6ed313/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:57:39Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:57:39Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(deploy): add the deployment plan and point CLAUDE.md at it\n\nDeploy.md is the authority for taking this online. It records the three\ndecisions taken (real models via hosted APIs, a login gate between landing\nand workbench, Railway), the platform constraints that were verified rather\nthan assumed, the invariants this workstream may not break, five PRs with\nbinding acceptance criteria, and a findings register.\n\nTwo things about the register are deliberate. Every row carries a file:line\nso it can be checked instead of believed, and each row is marked `direct`\n(confirmed in-session by reading the file or resolving the compose config)\nor `audit` (reported with a citation by a code-audit pass, not\nindependently re-checked). Treating those two as the same kind of claim is\nhow a plan acquires facts nobody verified.\n\nThe register is not a second backlog. Final_Report.md keeps the single\noutstanding-work list for the product; Deploy.md covers only what blocks\ndeployment, and where an item is both it gets struck from Outstanding Work\nin the PR that fixes it.\n\nThe constraint that outranks the rest is model parity: every figure the UI\nand the docs display is generated from results/eval-h1-repeat3-2026-07-31/\nand is a claim about that exact configuration. All three of its models are\navailable as hosted APIs, so the deployment can match it without\nsubstituting anything — and if a future change substitutes one, it says so\non the landing page and /methodology or it reverts.\n\nCLAUDE.md gets a pointer, not a copy: §2 carries only the seven invariants\nthat stay true whichever PR is in flight, and says explicitly that the\nbacklog lives in Deploy.md. Three copies of \"what''s left\" is the drift\npattern this project keeps having to fix. Sections renumbered 2-6 -> 3-7;\nthe two internal §1 references still resolve.","tree":{"sha":"0eb7cd1a201f53bf1d8e3898c6b0dc8f3fff0523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/0eb7cd1a201f53bf1d8e3898c6b0dc8f3fff0523"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/3b9f977bf74cf102b2f4b419e59e2a75dc6ed313","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"htt