ents","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:01:02Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:01:02Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"Merge pull request #17 from Odiethebest/docs/interview-resume-assets\n\ndocs(interview): data inventory and bilingual resume material","tree":{"sha":"2653131344c4bc83ea7d006c6907c52a09956753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/2653131344c4bc83ea7d006c6907c52a09956753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGE0NjEyYjg3MWVkMGJhMGM3MjYzMGIwNGRkOTk5YmRmYWRkZGEwZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776","sha":"11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51","sha":"ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51"}],"sha":"a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/a4612b871ed0ba0c72630b04dd999bdfaddda0f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:55:44Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:55:44Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(interview): add bilingual resume material with a per-figure usage guide\n\nThe same facts as the technical brief, reorganised for a mentor who will\nedit a resume and who reads once. Chinese and English are complete\nindependently rather than one being a translation of the other.\n\nFigures come only from the brief''s §4 ledger and the data inventory. Where\nthe ledger attaches a qualifier, the text either carries it or uses a\nphrasing that does not need one.\n\nLead order is deliberate: citation verification, then how the agent is kept\nin check, then the evaluation methodology. The call graph does not open,\nbecause my own control arm measured it down and opening with it means\nopening on the weakest link. The non-ML boundary is stated outright -- no\ntraining, no loss, no RL, every model an off-the-shelf call, and the static\ncall-graph resolution labelled as program analysis.\n\nTwo Mermaid diagrams, drawn only from components that exist. `chunks.tsv`\nand `index_runs` are dashed and marked NOT WIRED so nobody reads them as\npart of the data flow.\n\nThe section that makes this usable is \"what each number proves\", in three\ngroups. Group one is safe on a resume, with a column saying what each\nfigure means to a reader rather than restating the figure. Group two lists\nthe qualifier each number needs and the specific follow-up question that\nlands if it is missing. Group three stays verbal, with the reason it stays\noff the resume: needs full context, is a diagnostic excluded from the\nverdict, is configuration a reader cannot judge, or is not an outcome.\n\nBullets carry only ledger-backed figures or mechanistic results. There are\nno throughput, latency, token-cost or accuracy-lift numbers, and the notes\nto my mentor explain per category why adding any would mean inventing them.\nSix phrasings that collapse under the first follow-up are listed as\nmust-not-reintroduce, since an editing pass would otherwise restore them.\n\nTwo disclosures are written where they cannot be missed. Filtering test\ncode also mechanically moves the metric toward the ground truth, and the\ncommit that made the change says so; I have to say it first rather than\nhave it read out of the commit. And the citation counts come from\nsingle-baseline runs carrying no verdict, whose own report says the counts\nare the evidence and the means are weak, so the means are never quoted.\n\nSeven bullets is too many for one resume, so the file ends with a\nby-channel selection instead of a deletion: four for technical\napplications, three for HR screens, with a reason for each.","tree":{"sha":"2653131344c4bc83ea7d006c6907c52a09956753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/2653131344c4bc83ea7d006c6907c52a09956753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGNlMjcyZmViN2NjOTI1MjMyZmQ4Yzc5MDRlM2IwZTQxZGE2MzBmNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4","sha":"2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4"}],"sha":"ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ce272feb7cc925232fd8c7904e3b0e41da630f51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:55:26Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:55:26Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(interview): audit which ledger figures are unused and which changes have a before and after\n\nA read-only pass over the brief''s §4 ledger and the git history, answering\ntwo questions: which quotable figures have not reached the resume material,\nand which changes can be told as \"I made a change, here is the outcome\".\n\nLedger usage, 77 rows: 46 already used, 23 unused but safe, 8 unused and\nunsafe. Worth knowing that rows 2 and 3 -- the edge counts, the figure an\noutside reader would most readily take for a headline -- appear in the\nresume material only inside the forbidden-phrasings table, as an example of\nwhat not to write. That is deliberate.\n\nThe unused figures are re-tiered by whether they can carry a bullet on\ntheir own (A), need a qualifying sentence (B, interview ammunition only),\nor are scale figures (C). Tier C is completed from the whole repository\nrather than only from the ledger, since scale is what a non-technical\nreader reads first and the resume material used it least.\n\nImprovement chains are only counted when all four elements are present: a\nsourced before-state, a change with a file:line or commit, a sourced\nafter-state, and causality recorded in code or in a commit rather than\ninferred afterwards. Each is classified, and the classification is the\npoint:\n\n- Engineering, 4. Unifying the symbol-resolution rule (verified citations\n  48-54 -> 62-67, redaction markers 17-21 -> 9-13, symbol-form citations\n  surviving for the first time). Hydrating graph evidence (L3 call-graph\n  contribution -0.0067 -> +0.0226). Filtering test code out of retrieval\n  (47% of retrieved candidates -> 0%). And call resolution, where the\n  commit measured the downstream effect itself and recorded it as zero --\n  that one cannot be told as an outcome.\n- Measurement correction, 5. Symmetric scoring, the GRAPH_TOOLS set, the\n  B3.5 arm, dropping groundedness from the composite, and scoring an\n  uncited answer zero.\n- Parameter change, 4. One of them is unusable: the comment behind the\n  rerank passage cap quotes latency figures that were observed once and\n  never benchmarked, and this project quotes no latency anywhere.\n\nEngineering chains are few and that is the project''s shape rather than a\ngap in the search. The dense iteration is almost entirely about how things\nare measured. Measurement corrections are not moved into the engineering\ncolumn to improve the ratio -- calling one an optimisation invites \"how\nmuch did it improve\", and the honest answer is that the metric did not\nmove, the earlier measurement was wrong.\n\nSeven chains are listed separately as \"suspected, evidence incomplete\" so\nthey stay out of the resume material.","tree":{"sha":"c130a2053965d2682d84ac8845a7061edad6b5f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/c130a2053965d2682d84ac8845a7061edad6b5f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/2e1c41a368e99c1861fd231240300be10dffd5b4","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDJlMWM0MWEzNjhlOTljMTg2MWZkMjMxMjQw