web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDExZDBiNjdhYWMyODhiZTkwNDdkNzBjNmE1MjgzMDkyYzcyZDA3NzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/0eaa3212dcdc65966e242e1c900c665b9d79570b","sha":"0eaa3212dcdc65966e242e1c900c665b9d79570b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/0eaa3212dcdc65966e242e1c900c665b9d79570b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a","sha":"9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a"}],"sha":"11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/11d0b67aac288be9047d70c6a5283092c72d0776"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T07:06:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T07:06:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(interview): add a role-specific prep document for LLM/agent engineering\n\nSame facts as DCODE_TECH_BRIEF.md, reorganised by what a hiring side\nactually evaluates rather than by how the system is built. The brief stays\nthe source of truth; this is a view over it, and appendix B maps every\nsection back so a follow-up question can be traced.\n\nNarrative order is deliberate: honesty contract -> bounded-agent control\n-> evaluation methodology. The call graph is not the opener. It is the part\nmy own ablation measured down, so leading with it means opening on the\nweakest link; its correct place is as evidence that I do not overrate a\ncomponent because I spent effort on it.\n\nThe non-ML boundary is stated explicitly rather than left ambiguous. There\nis no training, no loss, no RL, no fine-tuning -- every model is an\noff-the-shelf call. The static call-graph resolution has real difficulty\nbut it is program analysis, not machine learning, and section 3.5 answers\n\"is this an algorithms project?\" with \"no\" and then gives the positioning\nI do stand behind: evaluation and verifiability infrastructure for agents,\nwhich is an upstream dependency of the training side rather than a\nsubstitute for it.\n\nTwo defects carried over from the brief are fixed here, and appendix C\nrecords all seven such corrections:\n\n- \"multi-step evidence gathering is six times the call graph\" only holds\n  on L3 (+0.1466 against +0.0226). On L2 the two are indistinguishable\n  (+0.0221 against +0.0218, a ratio of 1.01). Every occurrence of \"six\n  times\" now carries the L3 qualifier, and the cheat sheet''s ablation\n  table lists both rows so the L2 line cannot be dropped by accident.\n- The brief''s eight-minute version quoted httpx figures that were not in\n  its own ledger. They are now measured and added to appendix A at level\n  D, with the constraints that make them safe to say: 963 is the sum of\n  four edge types (calls is 398), the figures depend on a running Postgres\n  and cannot be checked from the repo, and they enter no conclusion.\n\nAlso new: a section on what to say when a number will not come to mind,\nwhich substitutes derivation and magnitude for the exact value -- the\nfailure mode it addresses is going vague under pressure, which reads worse\nthan saying how the number is computed and offering to look it up.","tree":{"sha":"90c8f8e6d1db8a9ebc4617b3624ca50f86a7dbc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/90c8f8e6d1db8a9ebc4617b3624ca50f86a7dbc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDlmYWEyNzkwODgyMGVjYmVjYjk1NzUwMThiNDdmY2I4OTAxZTc5MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d","sha":"23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d"}],"sha":"9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/9faa27908820ecbecb9575018b47fcb8901e791a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T06:09:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T06:09:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(interview): add a from-code technical brief\n\n1235 lines rebuilt from the source, not from the existing docs. Every\nfigure and every file:line was re-executed before being written down, and\neach number carries a source level: A = committed artifact field, B =\ncommitted source constant, C = recomputed this pass, D = depends on the\nrunning Postgres or the local .env and cannot be checked from the repo.\n\nStructure: current-state inventory; both end-to-end chains hop by hop with\nthe cross-boundary points marked; the nine core algorithms in\nintuition -> LaTeX -> code mapping -> parameters -> complexity -> failure\nmodes; a quotable-number ledger where every row also carries the sentence\nthat must be said alongside it; and an unquotable list for the figures that\nare structurally misleading on their own.\n\nFour things the audit turned up that the docs did not have:\n\n- `chunks.tsv` and its GIN index are written by nothing. Sparse retrieval\n  is application-level Okapi BM25. The column is a leftover, not a feature.\n- `@overload` stubs shadow real definitions. `_build_symbols` dedupes by\n  qualified name and keeps the first record, which is the first overload\n  stub -- 9 symbols and 20 chunks (2.8%) point at a three-line `...` body.\n  Verified live: `iter_slices` resolves to line 614, not 621.\n- The recorded run ran on an older call graph. Re-running the current\n  worker code offline over the same corpus produces 316 call edges against\n  the 303 in the database (+4.3%); the other three edge types are\n  identical, which localises the difference to call resolution alone.\n- The call-edge funnel, measured rather than asserted: 2615 ast.Call sites\n  visited, 316 resolved, 12.1%. The largest unresolved class is 1076\n  `obj.X()` receivers with no known type -- the capability this analysis\n  explicitly declines.\n\nAppendix A carries 25 drift entries with a suggested fix for each. Two of\nthem were closed while writing this: the taxonomy x source confound (see\nthe preceding commit) and the missing provenance for the a11y live-region\nregression, which git bisects to 09e2446 adding it and 7bc6abe removing it\nwith the retired query page.\n\nRead-only pass: no code, no evaluation artifact and no run was touched\nbeyond the one limitations entry committed separately.","tree":{"sha":"68afa4659a5102c3db6300814eb16985ad0799a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/68afa4659a5102c3db6300814eb16985ad0799a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDIzNTY4ZjRmMWViZWE1YmZiMTczZTBhZmE3YjJjNDI4OGRiYzNkOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/f5d0088d2baeb174a7226bf328db53420cb4745b","sha":"f5d0088d2baeb174a7226bf328db53420cb4745b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/f5d0088d2baeb174a7226bf328db53420cb4745b"}],"sha":"23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/23568f4f1ebea5bfb173e0afa7b2c4288dbc3d8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/f5d0088d2baeb174a7226bf328db53420cb4745b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T06:09:30Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T06:09:30Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(eval): record the taxonomy x source confound in the run''s limitations\n\nFound during a from-code audit of the recorded run, not during the run.\nAll 5 L1 questions are `manual`; all 17 `graph_reverse` questions are L2 or\nL3, and their ground-truth sets are about twice as large (mean 4.29 targets\nacross 2.94 files, against 2.12 across 1.38). So \"B4 leads on L3\" and \"B4\nleads on the reverse-constructed batch\" are not distinguishable with this\nsuite -- the two dimensions are collinear.\n\nMeasured, so the entry states a direction rather than only a worry: the\ngraph''s isolated margin (B4 - B3.5) is +0.028 on the manual L2/L3 subset\nagainst +0.018 on `graph_reverse`, and the share of questions citing at\nleast one graph-origin chunk is 9/16 manual against 10/17 `graph_reverse`.\nThe confound does not appear to run in the direction that would flatter B4.\nThe entry says explicitly that this measures whether the questions that\nexist favour the graph, and cannot measure the flows the graph misses.\n\nPrefixed ADDED AFTER THE RUN because line 2 of this file claims it was\nrecorded immediately after the process completed, and that claim has to\nstay true. Nothing was re-executed: the figures are recomputed from bytes\nalready in this directory and no recorded metric changed.\n\nSafe against the artifact drift check: provenance.json is not harness\noutput (dcode_eval.run writes six other files), and\nscripts/sync_eval_artifacts.py reads only `display`,\n`groundedness_guardrail`, `verdict_written_at` and `sparse_retrieval` from\nit -- never `limitations`. `make lint` passes.","tree":{"sha":"506d097df2314f35dfe816f99a5d350048d91767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/506d097df2314f35dfe816f99a5d350048d91767"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/f5d0088d2baeb174a7226bf328db53420cb4745b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api