+Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-31T23:24:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/371e28c4ac6bb5d0709caa66ca1e3f9d156850cc","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDM3MWUyOGM0YWM2YmI1ZDA3MDljYWE2NmNhMWUzZjlkMTU2ODUwY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/912e56348cc940bf90779e768c29147a0eec017a","sha":"912e56348cc940bf90779e768c29147a0eec017a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/912e56348cc940bf90779e768c29147a0eec017a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3","sha":"864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3"}],"sha":"371e28c4ac6bb5d0709caa66ca1e3f9d156850cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/371e28c4ac6bb5d0709caa66ca1e3f9d156850cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T23:00:03Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T23:00:03Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"eval: measure B0 against the live GitHub index\n\nCloses the oldest open item in the report. B0 file-level Recall@5 is\n0.308, against 0.776-0.829 for every in-house arm; on architecture\nquestions 0.111 against 0.632-0.799.\n\nThe first attempt scored 0.253 with L3 at exactly 0.000, and that was our\nfault. The keyword extractor sent \"Explain\" as a required term and GitHub\nANDs every term, so all 17 expansion questions -- which all open with that\nword -- matched nothing. Reporting that zero would have been a strawman\ndressed as a finding. The extractor now leads with identifiers (backticked\nsymbols, snake_case, CamelCase, dotted paths) and sends at most three\nterms, which is what a competent user of code search would type. B0 rose\nto 0.308 and L3 to 0.111: the baseline was made stronger on purpose, at\nour own expense, and a test pins that prose scaffolding never reaches the\nAPI again.\n\n12 of 33 questions still return nothing. That one is real -- keyword\nsearch against natural-language architecture questions -- not the query\nbuilder.\n\nRecorded in its own directory because it does not belong in a run it did\nnot participate in, and excluded from the drift check because it is the\nonly figure here that cannot be regenerated from committed bytes: it\nqueries a live index that re-crawls and re-ranks. The generator emits it\nas `null` when the directory is absent, so an unmeasured baseline stays a\nvisible blank rather than a zero.\n\nThe comparison against the current run was derived from that run''s already\nrecorded retrieved_files. No arm was re-executed and its artifacts were\nleft untouched.\n\nThe landing row still shows no bar for B0, now for a better reason: the\nladder plots nDCG over chunks and B0 has no chunk-level result. It states\nthe file-level figure and that the source is external and not\nreproducible. And the report says plainly that beating keyword search is\nnot a strong claim -- B0 is the floor, not a rival.","tree":{"sha":"ed429b9b9212e9fb4f1d804e5d39b7ef8807d11e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/ed429b9b9212e9fb4f1d804e5d39b7ef8807d11e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDg2NDUyNWQ1ZTM1OTEyNDAxNmE5MDM5ZThhNjgyYmE4ZTdiMzkwZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f","sha":"57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f"}],"sha":"864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/864525d5e359124016a9039e8a682ba8e7b390f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:38:15Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:38:15Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"eval: score every arm at file level and make B0 measurable\n\nB0 could not have produced a real number before this. Three reasons, all\nof which would have recorded a fabricated failure rather than a\nmeasurement.\n\nIts chunk ids were random UUIDs. Every chunk-level metric was therefore\npinned at 0.000 by construction -- verified: a result returning exactly\nthe right file still scores recall 0.0, mrr 0.0. Now a deterministic\nUUID5 of the path, which still cannot match ground truth but makes two\nruns diff-able.\n\nIt has no chunk-level result to give. Checked against a live response:\nGitHub''s code search returns a path, a matched fragment and character\noffsets within that fragment, and no line number anywhere. Synthesising a\nchunk from that would credit the baseline with a precision it does not\nhave. So the harness now computes file-level Recall/MRR/nDCG for every\narm from data it already recorded, and B0 is compared in the unit it\nactually retrieves in. Reported beside the decision, never inside it: the\nH1 composite stays chunk-level and B0 stays out of the decision.\n\nDistinct files present in the top-k, not the top-k distinct files. A\nchunk-level arm can spend several slots on one file while B0 spends one\nslot per file; that difference is a real property of chunk granularity\nand gets reported rather than normalised away.\n\nThe rate limit was wrong. Code search allows 10 req/min authenticated,\nnot the 30 the rest of the Search API allows, so a 33-question suite at\n2s spacing trips 403 partway through and the remaining questions score\nzero -- indistinguishable, in the artifact, from a baseline result.\n\nAnd with no token it now raises instead of returning an empty list that\nscores zero. An unmeasured baseline is an honest blank; a zero is a claim\nabout GitHub Search that we have not earned.","tree":{"sha":"56a18f8b9e054e2ebb8008635a3fcb546d215562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/56a18f8b9e054e2ebb8008635a3fcb546d215562"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDU3Yzk1NDJmNDU1NmM4ZWI2Y2FkZWZlOTcyYzk2MjJjNzU1YjQwNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d","sha":"433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d"}],"sha":"57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/57c9542f4556c8eb6cadefe972c9622c755b406f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:30:20Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:30:20Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs(env): document GITHUB_TOKEN for the B0 baseline\n\nOnly apps/eval reads it, via os.environ. Public-repo code search needs no\nscopes; the token exists to raise the rate limit, so issue one with nothing\nticked.\n\nRecords the two things that make B0 unlike every other figure here: left\nempty it reports unmeasured rather than zero, because an unmeasured\nbaseline is an honest blank while a zero is a claim about GitHub Search we\nhave not earned; and its result cannot be regenerated from committed bytes\nsince it queries a live external index.","tree":{"sha":"afcb8b0ad2bbbaa2928930c53ecd01a6747e31c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/afcb8b0ad2bbbaa2928930c53ecd01a6747e31c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDQzM2M1MDBjZWUzMmY5ZjZmNjc5ZmQxY2RkM2Y4NWU4MTYxNTA5OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec","sha":"19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec"}],"sha":"433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/433c500cee32f9f6f679fd1cdd3f85e81615099d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:17:48Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:17:48Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"eval: record the 3-repeat run and report H1 by level\n\nThe current verdict. Five arms including the B3.5 ablation, the frozen\n33-question suite, three repeats averaged, under the composite and repeat\nprotocol declared in the previous commit.\n\nH1 is unsupported. It is a conjunction of four comparisons and three\nclear: architecture questions beat both rivals by 3.4x and 4.9x the bar in\nall three repeats; cross-file beats dense RAG by 2.7x and falls 0.006\nshort against hybrid+rerank.\n\nThe finding that matters more than the verdict: across three identical\nrepeats the L2 margin was +0.038, +0.006 and +0.088 -- a range of 0.083,\nwider than the 0.050 bar -- and repeat 3 returned `supported` on its own.\nRepeat 3 cleared because B3 dropped 0.053 that run, not because B4\nimproved. Every single-run near-miss in this repository''s history sits\ninside that range, including two that would have read as passes.\n\nSurfaces now report H1 by level instead of by one word. The per-level\n`supported` flags are part of the pre-registered output, not a reading\nadded afterwards, and three of four cells clear -- stating only the\nconjunction states less than the run measured. The landing card shows all\nfour margins with their multiples of the bar, plus the repeat spread,\nbecause a mean margin without its spread claims a precision this suite\ndoes not have.\n\nProse corrected where the data moved under it, which was most of it. The\ncall graph is now +0.022/+0.023 rather than negative, and B3.5 attributes\n+0.147 on L3 to the agent loop instead -- the page previously said the\nablation that would separate them did not exist. The BM25 ladder claim\ninverted too: sparse no longer out-recalls hybrid on either H1 level now\nthat test code is excluded, and the one surviving inversion (B1 over B2 on\nL3, by 0.008) is reported rather than dropped with the rest.\n\nGuardrail tests repointed at the new truths, including one that had been\nasserting L3 was fragile relative to a bar it now clears.","tree":{"sha":"6ad2db4632e0bff7b36f73f36821d84688177f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/6ad2db4632e0bff7b36f73f36821d84688177f77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDE5Mjg5YzVmODYwOGI4YjdiNDNjOGFkNzdhMTc1OTZjYTE0MTNiZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa","sha":"38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa"}],"sha":"19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19289c5f8608b8b7b43c8ad77a17596ca1413bec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T19:28:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T19:28:17Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"eval: drop groundedness from the composite, average 3 repeats\n\nDeclared and committed BEFORE the run it judges. That ordering is the only\nthing separating this from picking a rule that produces the answer we\nwant, and it is verifiable from this commit''s position in the history --\nwhich is why it is its own commit, made while no run exists under it.\n\nTHE COMPOSITE. Three retrieval terms; groundedness is reported and gated\nat >=0.95 beside the decision, not inside it.\n\nOn the merits: groundedness is 1.000 for every arm, on every level, in\nevery run so far. A term identical across arms adds no discrimination and\nonly dilutes margins, and Technical_Design already called it \"reported\nseparately from that executable decision\" while it sat inside the\ncomposite.\n\nAgainst, said just as plainly: because the removed term is identical\nacross arms, dropping it multiplies every margin by exactly 4/3. Requiring\na three-term margin >= 0.050 is arithmetically identical to requiring a\nfour-term margin >= 0.0375. This is a 25% lower bar. Calling it a metric\ncorrection would be false.\n\nAnd the part that matters: four runs preceded this decision, missing by\n0.0036 (L3, v3) and 0.0016 (L2, v4). The change was found while looking\nfor those margins, not derived from a principle and then applied. Every\nh1_report now carries the four-term reading under `four_term` so the\ndifference needs no recomputation to see.\n\nOne consequence, pinned by a test: groundedness was the only channel on\nwhich an arm could win by being more truthful rather than by retrieving\nbetter, and it no longer moves the decision at all. Moot today at 1.000\neverywhere -- but that is a fact about the data, not the rule, and the\nrule is what future runs inherit. A fixture that had been passing on that\nchannel alone was rewritten to earn its margin from evidence instead.\n\nREPEATS. --repeats N runs the suite N times and judges the mean;\nper-question metrics are averaged first, then aggregated, and each\nrepeat''s own verdict is recorded under per_repeat so a disagreement\nbetween them is visible rather than smoothed. Retrieval is deterministic,\nsynthesis is not, and across four single runs the level that cleared the\nbar changed twice and moved by more than the bar itself.","tree":{"sha":"f536a2174d9db20c0fb40f0d39883667f71ac5c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/f536a2174d9db20c0fb40f0d39883667f71ac5c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDM4ZjgwMzY5MWVkNWQ3MmQzZTA4NjBjOGMxNThmMmYyYzNiNmZlYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267","sha":"4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267"}],"sha":"38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/38f803691ed5d72d3e0860c8c158f2f2c3b6feaa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:38:53Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:38:53Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(retrieval): stop answering implementation questions with test code\n\nMeasured on the 2026-07-31 suite: 47% of retrieved candidates and between\n26% and 48% of cited evidence came from tests/, in every arm. Asked \"how\ndoes Requests turn cookies into a Cookie header\", the product was showing\npeople test_requests.py. That is broken independently of any hypothesis.\n\nTests stay indexed and stay reachable: the filter lifts when the question\nmentions tests, and that check is deliberately generous, because\nwithholding test code from someone who asked for it is the worse failure.\n\nBinary, with no weight to tune. A \"tests are worth 0.7 of a real file\"\nscore adjustment would be a hyper-parameter, and one fitted on an\nevaluation set whose ground truth contains no test files at all. Filtering\nhappens after ranking, so the candidate pool and the fusion arithmetic are\nuntouched -- only what reaches the caller changes.\n\nApplied in the shared search path, so every arm gets it. Whether it moves\nB4 - B3 in either direction is not knowable in advance; it was not chosen\nfor that.\n\nDisclosure, because it matters more than the fix: this was found while\nlooking for the 0.0036 by which L3 missed the bar, and no ground-truth\nfile lives under tests/, so the change moves toward the ground truth. Both\nfacts are recorded here and in the report rather than left for a reader to\nnotice.","tree":{"sha":"918ace69d09dcd051a68ecef0e9ee978adcfbc6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/918ace69d09dcd051a68ecef0e9ee978adcfbc6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDRjYjg2NjAwMGNhMWNlNWEyZjkxNTY4NzkzNGFlYmI3ZmMyZDQyNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694","sha":"d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694"}],"sha":"4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/4cb866000ca1ce5a2f915687934aebb7fc2d4267"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:55:52Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:55:52Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(worker): resolve inherited and locally-constructed call targets\n\nTwo call shapes the AST analysis could not see, both of which the\narchitecture questions run straight through.\n\nA `self.method()` defined on a base class resolved to nothing, because the\ncandidate was only ever `{module}.{this_class}.{attr}`. In requests that\nhides the entire redirect machinery from Session: resolve_redirects,\nrebuild_auth and friends live on SessionRedirectMixin. Inheritance is now\ncomputed before calls and the lookup walks declared bases breadth-first,\nnearest definition winning.\n\n`p = PreparedRequest()` followed by `p.prepare(...)` resolved to nothing.\nOnly a direct construction counts, so the class is read from the code\nrather than inferred; a name assigned two different classes is dropped\ninstead of guessed at. The \"no type inference\" limit is intact.\n\nMeasured on the indexed requests source: 267 -> 279 call edges. Small, but\nthe twelve are load-bearing ones -- prepare_body -> _encode_files,\nSession.send -> resolve_redirects, Session.prepare_request ->\nPreparedRequest.prepare.\n\nHonest limit, measured before claiming otherwise: this unlocks ZERO\nadditional end-to-end L3 ground-truth chains. Most of those chains end at\nan exception class or a class constructor, which are raised or\ninstantiated rather than called, so no `calls` edge can reach them; others\ncross `adapter.send(...)`, which needs real return-type inference. The\nbase walk is also an approximation of the MRO, not the MRO -- it ignores\nC3 linearisation and can pick the wrong sibling in a diamond.\n\nNot active in any recorded run yet: it needs a re-index, and re-indexing\nmid-comparison would move the corpus underneath the v1/v2 results.","tree":{"sha":"70e55c1ef6e0848054a89f18638d3261a5d4937e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/70e55c1ef6e0848054a89f18638d3261a5d4937e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGQ2MTNjYWE3NjA0Y2RiZWM0NjMzZTUxYjhmNTgzMTE5MDY0Zjc2OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988","sha":"2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988"}],"sha":"d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/d613caa7604cdbec4633e51b8f583119064f7694"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:49:59Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T17:49:59Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(agent): let graph evidence carry code and compete on relevance\n\nThe v2 run measured the call graph at -0.007 on architecture questions:\nthe no-graph arm beat the full arm. This is the diagnosed cause, in three\nparts, all system changes -- no metric, threshold or question was touched.\n\nGraph results reached the answer prompt as bare `file:line` names while\nretrieved chunks reached it with source. The structural half of B4''s\nevidence was literally uncitable prose. GET /internal/get_chunks hydrates\nthem from the chunk_id the graph tools already return.\n\nEvidence was ordered by which tool happened to run, never by relevance, so\nlow-value graph hits displaced good retrieval inside a finite prompt. One\ncross-encoder now scores the union against the question. `graph_distance`\nand evidence origin are deliberately NOT ranking terms: a tunable \"prefer\ngraph results\" prior fitted on the eval set would be a hyper-parameter\nchosen to make the hypothesis pass. Origin stays recorded for diagnostics.\n\nThe context budget is one number shared by every arm. B3 never has more\nthan its five retrieved chunks, so it constrains B4 alone -- which is the\npoint: graph evidence earns a slot against retrieval instead of being\nappended for free. Past the budget a target keeps its ID and stays citable\nand verifiable; only its content is dropped.\n\nmax_steps 8 -> 14. B4 saturated the old cap (1 search + 3 read_file + 3\nfind_references left one step for get_file_outline, while the no-graph arm\nreached two on the same budget). The walk was ending at the cap rather\nthan at the planner''s decision.\n\nDegrades on failure rather than erroring: an unavailable reranker falls\nback to observation order, failed hydration leaves the target bare. Both\nare pinned by tests, as is the budget''s overflow behaviour and the fact\nthat ranking is by relevance rather than tool order.","tree":{"sha":"6185834254348e3658200d8090045085128d183d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/6185834254348e3658200d8090045085128d183d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDIzNzljMzlhYzg3NjkxODdjNjBmMDNhOWMzZTc1YThiZDI0YTQ5ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a","sha":"607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a"}],"sha":"2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/2379c39ac8769187c60f03a9c3e75a8bd24a4988"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:18:04Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:18:04Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs: pre-register criteria set 3 items 1-3 before any run\n\nCommitted while eval-h1-l3x12-2026-07-31 is still the current verdict and\nno suite has run under the new protocol, so the record shows the protocol\nwas fixed before any number under it existed. That ordering is the whole\nvalue of a pre-registration, and it is only verifiable from the commit\ngraph, so it gets its own commit.\n\nRecords the chosen rule and why final evidence beat candidate top-k, the\ntwo-axis mode table, why retrieval mode has to live in the tool args, the\nthree B3.5 contrasts and why B3.5 stays out of the pass criteria, and why\nread_file and get_file_outline are kept in B3.5 -- weakening it would\ninflate B4 - B3.5.\n\nAlso states plainly that the rule change is expected to move the verdict\nand that the direction is unknown. Saying so now costs nothing; saying it\nafterwards would be worthless.\n\nCLAUDE.md: the run is unblocked but is a deliberate act, so ask first, and\nrestart the agent container before it or dense_only/agent_no_graph return\n422 from a process holding the old literals.","tree":{"sha":"2aa9bdd3acbfb0506cd653c0f15eec80f1cb8a6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/2aa9bdd3acbfb0506cd653c0f15eec80f1cb8a6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDYwN2U0MWEyMDk2YjJlZjYyMDZkOTJiMzAxYjk3Y2VmMzcxOTMyM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2","sha":"b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2"}],"sha":"607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/607e41a2096b2ef6206d92b301b97cef3719323a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:18:04Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:18:04Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(eval): one official scoring rule for every decision arm\n\nCriteria set 3 item 1. Protocol uniform_final_verified_evidence_v2: the\nofficial metric is verified final evidence for B2, B3, B3.5 and B4 alike,\nreplacing v1''s B4-only special case.\n\nThis is the thing the last verdict actually turned on. Under v1, B4 - B3\non L3 was +0.045; scoring B3 by B4''s rule gave +0.051. The bar is 0.050.\nA decision that moves depending on which arm is measured how is not a\ndecision, so the choice is removed rather than resolved in whichever\ndirection reads better.\n\nChosen rule is final evidence, not candidate top-k, because top-k scores a\nlist the graph never touches -- the exact defect criteria set 2 was opened\nto fix. B0/B1 emit no citations, cannot be scored this way, and stay\nretrieval references outside the H1 decision. Every row still records\ncandidate_* and final_evidence_* side by side, so the alternative stays\nauditable without being selectable after the fact.\n\nB3.5 is written to h1_report under \"diagnostics\" and never into\n\"comparisons\". Promoting an arm into the decision rule would be changing\nthe pass criteria, which the standing commitments forbid. A test pins the\nexact key set of a comparison so that cannot drift.\n\nFixed before running anything under it: the rule change straddles the bar\nL3 missed by, and which way it moves is not knowable until the suite runs.","tree":{"sha":"61cf26eef805647aef0e315ade6ae9946c34a521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/61cf26eef805647aef0e315ade6ae9946c34a521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGIzOWU3NTZhMDk5ZGM1MGJmY2E5Mjk2OTE4NDc5NWI1OTE2NTlmYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf","sha":"ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf"}],"sha":"b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/b39e756a099dc50bfca92969184795b591659fb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:17:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:17:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(eval): route B2 through the agent and add the B3.5 arm\n\nB2 answered from a template, which fixed its groundedness at the constant\n1.0 -- a quarter of the composite the H1 decision is computed from,\nawarded rather than measured -- and left it emitting no citations at all,\nso no scoring rule could apply to B2 and B4 alike. It now answers via\ndense_only through the same agent path as B4.\n\nB3.5 is B4 with the call graph switched off. B4 - B3 moves when either the\ngraph or multi-step reading moves and cannot say which; B4 - B3.5 holds\nthe agent fixed and removes only the graph, which is the hypothesis.\nB3.5 - B3 is what multi-step reading is worth on its own.\n\nB1 deliberately keeps its template: it is a retrieval reference, not a\nsystem arm, and it is not in the H1 decision. Giving it a sparse_only mode\nwould make every displayed row one system with one variable, but it would\nalso stop B1 being a pure BM25 baseline. Left as an open choice in the\nreport rather than decided quietly here.\n\nOne test asserts each arm actually sends its own mode over the wire. All\nfour arms share one client helper, so a wiring slip there would run four\nidentically-configured arms and make the ladder meaningless while every\ntest that mocks at a higher level still passed.","tree":{"sha":"9441c2a6307eed527b45e9a03741d22637969ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/9441c2a6307eed527b45e9a03741d22637969ca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKGFlNzJkMTJmNWU3YWJkYzEzMzA0ZjMxYWRlYjE2OWU5NzQ1NzlkYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195","sha":"19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195"}],"sha":"ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/ae72d12f5e7abdc13304f31adeb169e974579dbf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:17:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:17:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"feat(agent): make the evaluation arm a two-axis mode\n\nCriteria set 3 items 2 and 3. AgentMode gains dense_only and\nagent_no_graph, and a single table maps every mode to (retrieval, tool\nexpansion). One synthesis model, prompt, citation protocol, guardrail and\nstep budget across all of them; only those two axes vary, and keeping the\nmapping in one place is what makes \"the arms are comparable\" checkable.\n\nsearch_code takes the retrieval mode as a tool ARGUMENT rather than reading\nit from state. The tool cache key is (tool, repo_id, args), so a mode held\noutside the args would have let B2''s dense search and B3''s hybrid search\nshare one cache entry -- two arms silently identical, with every\nhigher-level test still green.\n\nagent_no_graph (B3.5) removes find_definition, find_references,\nget_call_neighbors, get_dependencies and get_dependents from\nconsideration, and keeps read_file and get_file_outline.\n\nThe first draft of that gate stopped the walk at the first blocked tool.\nThat was wrong in a direction worth naming: branch ordering puts\nfind_references before get_file_outline, so B3.5 would never have reached\nthe outline tool, which understates the no-graph arm and therefore\noverstates the call graph in B4 - B3.5 -- an error that flatters the\nhypothesis under test. Structural candidates are now skipped, not\ntruncating.\n\nTests pin each mode''s opening retrieval, that no-expansion arms take\nexactly one step, that agent_no_graph never selects a structural tool\nacross five query shapes, that it still reaches get_file_outline, and --\nas the control that stops all of it passing vacuously -- that full mode\ndoes use the graph on the same query.","tree":{"sha":"22333dcb20226ca440ac4f1fe0f9b841838d43a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/22333dcb20226ca440ac4f1fe0f9b841838d43a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDE5MDYxNTc3ZWQ3Y2M1OGVhOGFjZWJkYmFkYWUyN2NmYzI3YTQxOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e","sha":"7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e"}],"sha":"19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/19061577ed7cc58ea8acebdbadae27cfc27a4195"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs: update the operational and constraint notes\n\nHonesty_Constraints gains a twelfth rule, earned by this run: when two\ndefensible scoring rules disagree about the outcome, publish the\npre-registered one as the verdict and the other beside it. Selecting the\nother one afterwards is indistinguishable from the outside from having\npre-registered it honestly, which is why the choice is not available after\nthe fact. Section 11 also now records that a *qualitative* claim can go\nstale -- the drift check only guards figures.\n\nOperations gains a step 0: flush Redis before a recorded run. Agent tool\nresults cache for 24h and a warm cache can serve graph results produced by\nolder agent code. Not hypothetical -- it cost this run a restart.\n\nCLAUDE.md''s standing constraint now points at criteria set 3 and says why\nre-running the current protocol unchanged cannot conclude anything.","tree":{"sha":"bf040465e6be2bd47c4baadf22a4072f58ec9569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/bf040465e6be2bd47c4baadf22a4072f58ec9569"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDdmYTM1ZDk3YmM4ZWFiZTNjNzM1YzEwNjcwMGZiYTdmOWRjMTgzOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770","sha":"991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770"}],"sha":"7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/7fa35d97bc8eabe3c735c106700fba7f9dc1838e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:47Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"fix(frontend): repoint the honesty guardrails at what is now true\n\nFive guardrail tests failed against the new run. Every one of them pinned\na claim the data had made false, so none is deleted -- each is repointed at\nthe claim that is now load-bearing.\n\n\"Never shows B4 beating B3, they tie\" cannot survive B4 leading, and the\npage should not pretend otherwise. What has to stay pinned is why the rows\ndiffer: identical retrieval, different scoring rules. A ladder showing B4\nahead without that sentence reads as a clean win the run did not produce.\n\n\"Frames the graph as unmeasured\" is inverted: the page now must state the\nmeasured contribution, and the test forbids the word \"unmeasured\" from\ncoming back.\n\n\"L3 fragile at n=3\" becomes an assertion that one question''s weight still\nexceeds the distance to the bar -- checked against the report rather than\nhardcoded, so it stays honest as n grows.\n\nThe BM25 ladder test now asserts sparse out-recalls hybrid on both H1\nlevels. On 33 questions that can no longer be waved away as one lucky\nlexical hit, and the copy says so.\n\nOne test is new: the page must publish that the verdict depends on the\nscoring rule. That sentence is the most omittable fact in this run, which\nis exactly why it gets a guardrail.","tree":{"sha":"108d0742db8020aa0350e58b063585cee5a56927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/108d0742db8020aa0350e58b063585cee5a56927"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/commits/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770","node_id":"C_kwDOS2E-LtoAKDk5MWNlYWViYTdjN2Y4NGZlYTdhMTllZGI5OGU0MDlkNzQ1Mjc3NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest/Dcode/commit/f915c7bfeb0c883c5d8477f7dff75542fc086a49","sha":"f915c7bfeb0c883c5d8477f7dff75542fc086a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/f915c7bfeb0c883c5d8477f7dff75542fc086a49"}],"sha":"991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/991ceaeba7c7f84fea7a19edb98e409d74527770"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135147367?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Odiethebest","id":135147367,"login":"Odiethebest","node_id":"U_kgDOCA4vZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Odiethebest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/commits/f915c7bfeb0c883c5d8477f7dff75542fc086a49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:31Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:56:31Z","email":"520yangziqi@gmail.com","name":"odieyang"},"message":"docs: rewrite the narrative the new numbers invalidated\n\nThe figures regenerate; the sentences around them do not. Three standing\nclaims were false as of this run and are replaced rather than softened.\n\n\"Why B4 could not beat B3\" is gone -- B4 does beat B3 on L2 now. \"The\ngraph''s contribution is unmeasured\" is gone; it is measured, at 4 new\nground-truth hits across 3 of 33 questions, and reporting that number is\nthe point of having built the measurement. \"L3 is fragile at n=3\" becomes\nfragile at n=12, for the sharper reason that one question outweighs the\n0.005 the level missed by.\n\nAdded, because omitting them would make the result read better than it is:\nthe verdict flips under symmetric scoring and both numbers are published;\nthe criteria-set-2 prediction that B4''s scoring rule handicaps B4 was\nfalsified and is left visible rather than edited out; B1/B2 groundedness\nis a template constant that is a quarter of their composite; the two H1\nlevels are not independent samples; 17 of 33 questions are reverse-\nconstructed from the graph under test.\n\nCriteria set 3 replaces set 2 as the gate: one scoring rule for every arm,\na dense_only mode so B2 can produce final evidence at all, and a B3.5\ndiagnostic arm -- diagnostic only, since adding an arm to the decision rule\nwould be changing the pass criteria.","tree":{"sha":"7158add63bcde17b9d5f36206b20746945809216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Odiethebest/Dcode/git/trees/7158add63bcde17b9d5f36206b20746945809216"},"url":"https://api.github.