d796dccdcc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/d3f877db08756e187437ef85b3135d796dccdcc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9740281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/karanjhaveri","id":9740281,"login":"karanjhaveri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NDAyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/ff0007a87bd076f5c83f062349ab817c4d137fd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:33:37Z","email":"karannj@hotmail.com","name":"Karan Jhaveri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:33:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: AWS-icon architecture diagram, freshness fixes, and naming consistency (#13)\n\nRefreshes the docs, standardizes the product name, and includes a small\nagent rename that keeps docs and runtime names aligned.\n\nDiagram & docs:\n- Replace the mermaid architecture block with a clean AWS reference-style\n  diagram (docs/assets/cloudops-architecture.svg); remove the old PNG.\n- Correct DEPLOY_MODE guidance in README + docs/development.md: it''s a\n  shared key (scripts/shared-keys.txt), so it must be passed as a CLI\n  override (DEPLOY_MODE=gateway-only make deploy-auto); a value in .env is\n  stripped by deploy.sh and silently ignored.\n- Freshness: 8 -> 9 AWS tools, unit-test count 415 -> 475.\n\nNaming consistency:\n- Standardize the product name to \"CloudOps Multi-Agent System\" across\n  README (title casing), docs, developer guide, agent prompts, Makefile,\n  pyproject, .env.example, bootstrap template, and package headers. A\n  prior change renamed only the README; this finishes the sweep.\n\nAgent rename:\n- lambda-runtime-upgrade-agent -> lambda-upgrade-agent in hierarchy.json\n  (entry key, ops-excellence children, routing prompt). The old runtime\n  name exceeded AgentCore''s 48-char cap under longer project prefixes; the\n  new name fits. The gateway tool name (lambda-runtime) is unchanged.\n- Rename docs/agents/lambda-runtime-upgrade.md -> lambda-upgrade.md and\n  update README references.\n\nNote: the agent-prompt edits invalidate all agent build hashes, so the\nnext deploy rebuilds all agent containers.\n\n78 agent/topology/prompt unit tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e91ae639ac05f3c29f124edce36005996ecae49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/trees/6e91ae639ac05f3c29f124edce36005996ecae49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/commits/ff0007a87bd076f5c83f062349ab817c4d137fd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e91ae639ac05f3c29f124edce36005996ecae49\nparent a78cbf5d06198ba7b52b8ea021f9f097386c4aa6\nauthor Karan Jhaveri <karannj@hotmail.com> 1784637217 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784637217 +0800\n\ndocs: AWS-icon architecture diagram, freshness fixes, and naming consistency (#13)\n\nRefreshes the docs, standardizes the product name, and includes a small\nagent rename that keeps docs and runtime names aligned.\n\nDiagram & docs:\n- Replace the mermaid architecture block with a clean AWS reference-style\n  diagram (docs/assets/cloudops-architecture.svg); remove the old PNG.\n- Correct DEPLOY_MODE guidance in README + docs/development.md: it''s a\n  shared key (scripts/shared-keys.txt), so it must be passed as a CLI\n  override (DEPLOY_MODE=gateway-only make deploy-auto); a value in .env is\n  stripped by deploy.sh and silently ignored.\n- Freshness: 8 -> 9 AWS tools, unit-test count 415 -> 475.\n\nNaming consistency:\n- Standardize the product name to \"CloudOps Multi-Agent System\" across\n  README (title casing), docs, developer guide, agent prompts, Makefile,\n  pyproject, .env.example, bootstrap template, and package headers. A\n  prior change renamed only the README; this finishes the sweep.\n\nAgent rename:\n- lambda-runtime-upgrade-agent -> lambda-upgrade-agent in hierarchy.json\n  (entry key, ops-excellence children, routing prompt). The old runtime\n  name exceeded AgentCore''s 48-char cap under longer project prefixes; the\n  new name fits. The gateway tool name (lambda-runtime) is unchanged.\n- Rename docs/agents/lambda-runtime-upgrade.md -> lambda-upgrade.md and\n  update README references.\n\nNote: the agent-prompt edits invalidate all agent build hashes, so the\nnext deploy rebuilds all agent containers.\n\n78 agent/topology/prompt unit tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX2chCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh5oQADCscpvpqSQsCUAfqEzoCVcZ\nJhi43+7UWjkcGJeQLW5Zveg54+qddc6PaefzMqlMm9Blv9UlYisFsCXrQtclR2QU\n45VQYVIXbGfcDzBP5lYlO7T+SMTYMbCfJNBZ7C7WkL2s8hK14xEmNZRlFWoKwrrs\nCsPSTXDzV4bd+5SVByo4kma2LYzOA2wy1V63om7fBytRHcRWYDElQ1V+GL6VvI/F\nV47f7URxyRS6bkY5ZzvBoeqbuSH/KqoYJz89ZWEkXTKRTOYApu9pUnVuPvwPPJN6\nzYjbPkzU6IZBU+nGLAY9NfdDEfsRcO/1mWxBKhpeAyFU6nKYIhPcKsoXuiGwYkFO\nIK03vxxrz2ZvHTsuJXqZ+dfHzeZBJ5bAzueBy5YmQY7Dip1oouXUn3giVytMxseI\nxcI5lyR+h30DBiDtG+0rwzIQibPNomAzsgdMH9+pqKSDDu6Ne8ge1FQR0IVZTzvY\nQfsQ+h/zyip+nKGNpDkcgFIsfQqiD7V