t.com/u/9740281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/karanjhaveri","id":9740281,"login":"karanjhaveri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NDAyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/a78cbf5d06198ba7b52b8ea021f9f097386c4aa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T05:47:12Z","email":"karannj@hotmail.com","name":"Karan Jhaveri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T05:47:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(unit): fix cross_account pollution + standardize unit-test setup (#12)\n\ntest_lambda_runtime_tool.py replaced shared.cross_account in sys.modules at\nmodule scope and never restored it, breaking all of test_cross_account.py in a\nfull `make test-unit` run. Replace with a scoped `cross_account_stub` fixture\n(monkeypatch.setitem, auto-restored).\n\nAlso standardize the unit suite so this class of drift is less likely:\n- add tests/unit/conftest.py: centralizes deterministic AWS test env (region +\n  dummy creds at import time) and auto-applies the `unit` marker to the whole\n  package, so `pytest -m unit` selects all of it.\n- drop now-redundant per-file AWS_REGION setdefaults + the lone pytestmark.\n- docs/development.md: add a \"Testing Conventions\" section codifying handler\n  loading, the no-global-sys.modules-stub rule, env handling, moto-vs-MagicMock,\n  and markers.\n\n488 unit+topology tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","tree":{"sha":"d01741f5585273494ef8217ab50bc3300b56cf1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/trees/d01741f5585273494ef8217ab50bc3300b56cf1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/commits/a78cbf5d06198ba7b52b8ea021f9f097386c4aa6","verification":{"payload":"tree d01741f5585273494ef8217ab50bc3300b56cf1c\nparent 6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323\nauthor Karan Jhaveri <karannj@hotmail.com> 1784612832 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784612832 +0800\n\ntest(unit): fix cross_account pollution + standardize unit-test setup (#12)\n\ntest_lambda_runtime_tool.py replaced shared.cross_account in sys.modules at\nmodule scope and never restored it, breaking all of test_cross_account.py in a\nfull `make test-unit` run. Replace with a scoped `cross_account_stub` fixture\n(monkeypatch.setitem, auto-restored).\n\nAlso standardize the unit suite so this class of drift is less likely:\n- add tests/unit/conftest.py: centralizes deterministic AWS test env (region +\n  dummy creds at import time) and auto-applies the `unit` marker to the whole\n  package, so `pytest -m unit` selects all of it.\n- drop now-redundant per-file AWS_REGION setdefaults + the lone pytestmark.\n- docs/development.md: add a \"Testing Conventions\" section codifying handler\n  loading, the no-global-sys.modules-stub rule, env handling, moto-vs-MagicMock,\n  and markers.\n\n488 unit+topology tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXwfgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0TsQAAbqsFlZ2rjs1wZ9UpySV1b2\nAY9StYbE+ZAD+T1nq8j2qGjMGQnNLZatn