927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323","sha":"6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323"}],"sha":"a78cbf5d06198ba7b52b8ea021f9f097386c4aa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/a78cbf5d06198ba7b52b8ea021f9f097386c4aa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9740281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/karanjhaveri","id":9740281,"login":"karanjhaveri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NDAyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karanjhaveri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T06:54:14Z","email":"karannj@hotmail.com","name":"Karan Jhaveri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T06:54:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(terraform): manage supervisor AGUI protocol natively, drop deploy-script workaround (#11)\n\nAWS provider v6.50.0 added AGUI as a native server_protocol enum on\naws_bedrockagentcore_agent_runtime (we have v6.52.0 locked), so the\ncoordinated deploy-script workaround is no longer needed.\n\n- agentcore-runtime: set protocol_configuration { server_protocol = \"AGUI\" }\n  and drop protocol_configuration from lifecycle.ignore_changes so TF manages it\n- terraform.sh: remove the pre-revert that flipped the frontend AGUI->HTTP\n  before every terraform op (provider no longer crashes reading AGUI)\n- sync.sh: remove the post-deploy AGUI-set in _sync_agent; the remaining\n  update_agent_runtime calls preserve the existing protocol (call is not partial)\n- versions.tf: pin aws >= 6.50.0 (the real enforcement; init fails loudly on older)\n- docs + test docstrings: replace \"AGUI protocol dance\" with a short runtime-protocol\n  note; hierarchy.json protocol field is vestigial (nothing reads it), left as \"http\"\n\nVerified: 444 unit + 13 topology tests pass; terraform fmt clean; make plan shows\n0 destroys and no protocol crash. Deployed in-place AND via full destroy+recreate on\ndev — supervisor comes up READY at AGUI natively with no protocol dance; smoke test\nstreams with zero 424s in both cases.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","tree":{"sha":"387b01335336a628c3be532a83b0b1d454ad93c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/trees/387b01335336a628c3be532a83b0b1d454ad93c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/commits/6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323","verification":{"payload":"tree 387b01335336a628c3be532a83b0b1d454ad93c7\nparent b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955\nauthor Karan Jhaveri <karannj@hotmail.com> 1784530454 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784530454 +0800\n\nfix(terraform): manage supervisor AGUI protocol natively, drop deploy-script workaround (#11)\n\nAWS provider v6.50.0 added AGUI as a native server_protocol enum on\naws_bedrockagentcore_agent_runtime (we have v6.52.0 locked), so the\ncoordinated deploy-script workaround is no longer needed.\n\n- agentcore-runtime: set protocol_configuration { server_protocol = \"AGUI\" }\n  and drop protocol_configuration from lifecycle.ignore_changes so TF manages it\n- terraform.sh: remove the pre-revert that flipped the frontend AGUI->HTTP\n  before every terraform op (provider no longer crashes reading AGUI)\n- sync.sh: remove the post-deploy AGUI-set in _sync_agent; the remaining\n  update_agent_runtime calls preserve the existing protocol (call is not partial)\n- versions.tf: pin aws >= 6.50.0 (the real enforcement; init fails loudly on older)\n- docs + test docstrings: replace \"AGUI protocol dance\" with a short runtime-protocol\n  note; hierarchy.json protocol field is vestigial (nothing reads it), left as \"http\"\n\nVerified: 444 unit + 13 topology tests pass; terraform fmt clean; make plan shows\n0 destroys and no protocol crash. Deployed in-place AND via full destroy+recreate on\ndev — supervisor comes up READY at AGUI natively with no protocol dance; smoke test\nstreams with zero 424s in both cases.\n\nCo-authored-by: Karan Jhaveri <karannj@amazon.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXcYWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjmcQAFqW2RiI/nQTw7RPd4wD2H83\ns2UJaISm0l4k/pzpbQQRJdgxzFZsoCrWtKYh2YNzkq3FzQdRS1ax4cXyiGtx+nV0\n+cK8bsAFDtUj1WTXL8hrOmbKZVXjQgM/jc1SdwgUo9SwihTi/L1IjNWa52dMup4V\nErHYLzcUqXAf9gWTeYTdfGpR7eW60mHhw8ShaEQL1y0Ovgism6eBtsBZzYv8BO88\n8qWkkoUYMkoW2JS7NX3UCyc1xC0h4mA0W1gR0RvEOhmq87ac+PvNlQeJN4B4GvQY\nbKTY7agz9emrwfdWa/RoAstXgRugpQIbHpyLsoRvejsgtyXzPY8Qy5NUY/g32dBh\nArrT6DlQeoDiNPNPoXzXVehqlDEwzaLimYRhdu4uYf/syaWzFPUD4toqNk6HVsd4\nt2a+eIeN1tEFKQPDun26749wbo8O14cIO7BIjG1BZN10kkBIlenJgbBAQK7WNtX6\nh26cMuLWPDGVKupPpdo4T68WNooQST53L2CNxu7kG4k70tkXoVEwq4mpDzrkzrMF\nNiMxy0vcoqvN4P2ev09yakO4n+tOJuyruURlgoTXEv+L8R0lXEo8d4qO+oXk62nX\nYG/OjUKFZ6zQ/W6/Hb2tMrPIDqHmpPnPJ6s9pwe0w/fiN991FlvXGy+yfJY//2Ll\nJqP1rV0g1qb0+KbFhyiZ\n=ZOLF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-20T06:54:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commit/6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323","node_id":"C_kwDOS2FF8NoAKDZlOWQyNDkyNzUyNmI2NDNlMmVkM2Y5NmVlODNmMTUxN2RhMWIzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commit/b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955","sha":"b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955"}],"sha":"6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/6e9d24927526b643e2ed3f96ee83f1517da1b323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81810237?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/higoyal01","id":81810237,"login":"higoyal01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODEwMjM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/higoyal01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/commits/b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T05:58:23Z","email":"higoyal@amazon.com","name":"Himanshu Goyal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T05:58:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(lambda-runtime): add Lambda runtime upgrade agent + MCP tool (#9)\n\nAdds a Lambda runtime upgrade capability to the Ops Excellence domain.\n\nNew agent (leaf/worker under ops-excellence-agent):\n  - lambda-runtime-upgrade-agent — discovers functions on deprecated/EOL\n    runtimes, analyzes code compatibility, and produces migration guidance\n    for Python, Node.js, Java, .NET, and Ruby.\n\nNew read-only MCP tool (lambda-runtime), 7 tools:\n  - discover_lambda_regions, list_functions_by_runtime,\n    get_function_configuration, get_function_code,\n    get_runtime_support_status, get_deprecated_functions,\n    get_deprecated_functions_multi_region.\n  - IAM: lambda:ListFunctions/GetFunction/GetFunctionConfiguration +\n    ec2:DescribeRegions (least-privilege, read-only).\n\nAlso:\n  - Report template (lambda_runtime_upgrade_report), dual-registered.\n  - 31 unit tests; per-leaf doc (docs/agents/lambda-runtime-upgrade.md);\n    README hierarchy/structure/doc-index updates.\n  - Minor: function_name_filter contains-match on list_functions_by_runtime,\n    RUNTIME_SUPPORT_DATA refresh-cadence comment, chart-axis labeling rule\n    in the agent prompt.","tree":{"sha":"bdb2d116d5259482374a5e9d3797f24acde1ae18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/trees/bdb2d116d5259482374a5e9d3797f24acde1ae18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aws-samples/sample-cloudops-multi-agent-system/git/commits/b66f2b6aea1368d70f2c9e3d74c654587f28b955","verification":{"payload":"tree bdb2d116d5259482374a5e9d3797f24acde1ae18\nparent fa81829c190a689d8c116c4a4599d1e87af11639\nauthor Himanshu Goyal <higoyal@amazon.com> 1784527103 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784527103 +0800\n\nfeat(lambda-runtime): add Lambda runtime upgrade agent + MCP tool (#9)\n\nAdds a Lambda runtime upgrade capability to the Ops Excellence domain.\n\nNew agent (leaf/worker under ops-excellence-agent):\n  - lambda-runtime-upgrade-agent — discovers functions on deprecated/EOL\n    runtimes, analyzes code compatibility, and produces migration guidance\n    for Python, Node.js, Java, .NET, and Ruby.\n\nNew read-only MCP tool (lambda-runtime), 7 tools:\n  - discover_lambda_regions, list_functions_by_runtime,\n    get_function_configuration, get_function_code,\n    get_runtime_support_status, get_deprecated_functions,\n    get_deprecated_functions_multi_region.\n  - IAM: lambda:ListFunctions/GetFunction/GetFunctionConfiguration +\n    ec2:DescribeRegions (least-privilege, read-only).\n\nAlso:\n  - Report template (lambda_runtime_upgrade_report), dual-registered.\n  - 31 unit tests; per-leaf doc (docs/agents/lambda-runtime-upgrade.md);\n    README hierarchy/structure/doc-index updates.\n  - Minor: function_name_filter contains-match on list_functions_by_runtime,\n    RUNTIME_SUPPORT_DATA refresh-cadence comment, chart-axis labeling rule\n    in the agent prompt.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXbj/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF