ons_url":"https://api.github.com/users/satyamyadav/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/satyamyadav","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/satyamyadav/zanto-rust/commits/1a139a82e94fa8c5fc4f33ab236d3b3c08066ad5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T11:17:23Z","email":"satyamyadav3@gmail.com","name":"Satyam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T11:17:39Z","email":"satyamyadav3@gmail.com","name":"Satyam"},"message":"feat(desktop): Artifact Hub — tabbed panel merging explorer + viewer\n\nReplace the explorer-then-preview ArtifactBrowser with an Artifact Hub: the\nright panel hosts a Library (Documents + Pinned views) plus a strip of open\nartifact tabs. Clicking a Library item opens/focuses its tab; the assistant''s\ndocuments open via an ''Open in panel'' button on the chat message (the bubble\ntoolbar is gone). The active tab carries the toolbar, so actions persist with\nthe view:\n- doc tab (unsaved): Save → becomes a stored tab in place.\n- stored tab: Save a copy / Reveal / Delete (inline confirm).\n- pinned view tab: re-renders the chart/table (no file actions).\n\nNew artifactHub store models open tabs (doc/stored/pinned) + active tab. The\nchat message keeps its content + an ''Open in panel'' button; all file actions\nmoved to the hub. ArtifactBrowser deleted.\n\nVerified in mock: open-in-panel → doc tab + Save toolbar → Save (stored, in\nLibrary, file toolbar) → Delete (inline confirm, removed); Library dedup\nfocuses existing tab; pinned views restored (R-7 green). UI suite 37 pass\n(C-7 pre-existing flake unrelated); pnpm check 0/0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5dc0cdffab5b0caee1db5d534906e6e115b7131d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/satyamyadav/zanto-rust/git/trees/5dc0cdffab5b0caee1db5d534906e6e115b7131d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/satyamyadav/zanto-rust/git/commits/1a139a82e94fa8c5fc4f33ab236d3b3c0